1
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:25,542
And so?

2
00:01:25,718 --> 00:01:28,016
And so,
I'm sitting there staring at him, right?

3
00:01:28,188 --> 00:01:31,385
He tells me to get my crunchy
fucking fucknuts the fuck out of there.

4
00:01:31,558 --> 00:01:32,991
You believe that shit?

5
00:01:33,159 --> 00:01:35,559
-You know what I said, right?
-No, what did you say?

6
00:01:38,832 --> 00:01:41,392
-Shit. "Okay."
-You fucking said, "Okay."

7
00:01:41,568 --> 00:01:43,058
I'm sure you did.

8
00:02:08,895 --> 00:02:10,920
Control Center,
this is Stillwell 1215.

9
00:02:11,364 --> 00:02:12,797
Go ahead, Stillwell 1215.

10
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:15,264
I'm about four cars
out of 57th Street station...

11
00:02:15,435 --> 00:02:17,198
...being delayed
by a red signal light.

12
00:02:19,606 --> 00:02:21,073
Should be green, Stillwell 1215.

13
00:02:21,241 --> 00:02:23,300
Yeah, tell me something
I don't already know.

14
00:02:24,110 --> 00:02:27,307
All right, roll through it slow,
extreme caution, per the rulebook.

15
00:02:38,925 --> 00:02:42,258
Yeah, cracked rail. Nine-hundred feet
from the east end of the platform.

16
00:02:42,428 --> 00:02:44,919
It's the goddamn cold.
Metal contracts, you know that.

17
00:02:45,098 --> 00:02:47,225
I got it, I got it.
How long it take to fix it?

18
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,493
Gotta put a plate on it. Two hours.

19
00:02:50,737 --> 00:02:53,433
Thank you. Make it an hour and a half,
I'll buy you a beer.

20
00:03:23,436 --> 00:03:26,701
Shit, G.B. I hate to see you
down here on the floor, man.

21
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:30,536
Temporary, baby. I'll be up there
behind the glass before you know it.

22
00:03:43,957 --> 00:03:45,288
I'm gonna need the R train...

23
00:03:45,458 --> 00:03:47,790
...to switch over
to the express tracks at 34th.

24
00:03:47,961 --> 00:03:49,952
-Which express tracks?
-The one that Q uses.

25
00:03:50,129 --> 00:03:53,189
Once they exit the 57th Street,
they can switch over to the F Line.

26
00:03:53,366 --> 00:03:54,458
Straight into Queens.

27
00:03:54,634 --> 00:03:58,070
Once they get to Queens, they switch
back at 36th Street to the R Line.

28
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:02,402
All you gotta do, suspend the W,
N and R will pick up the slack.

29
00:04:47,553 --> 00:04:49,043
I can't see where I gotta look.

30
00:04:49,222 --> 00:04:51,690
Unlock the door.
Do it now or I'll kill you. Do it.

31
00:04:53,726 --> 00:04:54,750
All right, all right.

32
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:17,043
Shut up and walk.

33
00:05:17,884 --> 00:05:19,545
First car, go.

34
00:05:30,029 --> 00:05:32,054
See? I told you I could do this.

35
00:05:32,665 --> 00:05:34,929
Big fucking deal,
you did what you said you'd do.

36
00:05:51,884 --> 00:05:53,749
All right.

37
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:56,388
Five minutes of peace.

38
00:05:59,459 --> 00:06:02,690
-Yeah!
-Nice!

39
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:04,727
-Nice.
-All right.

40
00:06:04,897 --> 00:06:06,455
There you go.

41
00:06:11,871 --> 00:06:13,600
I'm on the train and I still got you.

42
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:17,134
-You still got me?
-I got you. What are you doing?

43
00:06:17,310 --> 00:06:19,278
You still got me?

44
00:06:20,513 --> 00:06:22,777
Oh, my God.

45
00:06:27,687 --> 00:06:29,177
Baby? Baby?

46
00:07:25,411 --> 00:07:26,708
Give me the cutting key.

47
00:07:27,613 --> 00:07:29,171
Cutting key.

48
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:49,064
Control Center calling Pelham 123.
Come in, Pelham 123.

49
00:07:49,569 --> 00:07:52,197
Why did you stop?
You're all green ahead.

50
00:07:56,375 --> 00:07:59,401
Control Center calling Pelham 123.

51
00:08:00,279 --> 00:08:02,747
Control Center calling Pelham 123.

52
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:05,140
Why did you stop, 123?
You got green ahead.

53
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:07,183
It's okay.

54
00:08:08,254 --> 00:08:10,347
Life is simple now.

55
00:08:10,523 --> 00:08:12,821
You just gotta do what I say.

56
00:08:17,697 --> 00:08:19,392
Not now, okay?

57
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:35,742
Where are you from?

58
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:39,514
-Brooklyn.
-You lrish?

59
00:08:40,119 --> 00:08:41,143
Yeah.

60
00:08:41,854 --> 00:08:43,947
I thought so.

61
00:08:44,957 --> 00:08:47,687
Who's driving Pelham 123?

62
00:08:51,430 --> 00:08:53,159
Maybe something fell on the tracks.

63
00:09:39,145 --> 00:09:41,238
Wait. Are we going backwards?

64
00:09:56,796 --> 00:09:59,196
42nd Street tower,
I got a train wrong-railing...

65
00:09:59,365 --> 00:10:02,232
...on the southbound Lexington
Avenue Line just north of you.

66
00:10:03,836 --> 00:10:06,669
Listen up,
we need to stop and stay in-station.

67
00:10:06,839 --> 00:10:09,933
All southbound locals
just north of the 51st Street station.

68
00:10:10,109 --> 00:10:12,839
The operator on 123
is Jerry Pollard.

69
00:10:13,012 --> 00:10:15,947
I know Jerry Pollard.
I went to motorman school with Jerry.

70
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:19,744
Pelham 123,
come in to me, Pelham 123.

71
00:10:19,919 --> 00:10:22,410
Pelham 123, Jerry Pollard,
what's going on down there?

72
00:10:22,588 --> 00:10:25,853
This is Control Center.
What's going on, 123?

73
00:10:28,094 --> 00:10:31,825
Get an express train to go alongside
them, see what we see in the cab.

74
00:10:31,998 --> 00:10:35,434
Yeah, this is South Ferry 105. I can't
get my windshield wiper to turn on.

75
00:10:35,601 --> 00:10:39,037
South Ferry 105, there's a circuit
breaker right behind you for that.

76
00:10:39,205 --> 00:10:40,536
What's going on?

77
00:10:40,706 --> 00:10:42,537
Maestro, what's going on?

78
00:11:00,026 --> 00:11:01,084
-Cop.
-Excuse me.

79
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:03,626
-Fuck.
-Watch your backs. Watch your backs.

80
00:11:03,796 --> 00:11:05,286
When I say stop, stop it hard.

81
00:11:10,436 --> 00:11:11,960
-Transit Police.
-Stop.

82
00:11:25,151 --> 00:11:26,618
Everybody sit the fuck down!

83
00:11:28,821 --> 00:11:29,913
Down!

84
00:11:30,823 --> 00:11:32,085
Sit the fuck down!

85
00:11:32,258 --> 00:11:34,886
Jesus! We're getting reports
of gunshots down the tunnel.

86
00:11:35,061 --> 00:11:36,392
Sergeant Moran.

87
00:11:36,562 --> 00:11:39,087
-Delgado, let's call off that express.
-Got it.

88
00:11:41,967 --> 00:11:44,834
I'm gonna die.
I'm gonna fucking die, man.

89
00:11:45,004 --> 00:11:46,028
Come on! Hey.

90
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:49,003
Everybody up! By the window!
Come on, up, up, up!

91
00:11:49,175 --> 00:11:50,802
Stand up! Stand up! Come on!

92
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:57,015
Move it! Against the window!

93
00:11:58,350 --> 00:12:00,215
What the fuck is going on?

94
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:02,718
There was a cop. Bashkin shot him.

95
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:04,651
I think-- I think he's dead.

96
00:12:04,824 --> 00:12:07,224
Put Bashkin on
and find your fucking guts!

97
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:09,588
-Do it!
-Fuck.

98
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:13,960
-What happened?
-A cop. He's dead.

99
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,560
Put the conductor on.

100
00:12:17,303 --> 00:12:19,396
-What's your name, conductor?
-Regina.

101
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:22,040
Regina, baby, listen,
you got a job to do, honey.

102
00:12:22,208 --> 00:12:23,232
A job?

103
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:26,310
God put you on this Earth
for one thing and one thing only.

104
00:12:26,479 --> 00:12:28,447
You conduct those people
off the train...

105
00:12:28,614 --> 00:12:31,139
...up to the platform.
You got that? Let me hear it.

106
00:12:31,317 --> 00:12:32,841
Let me hear you do that.

107
00:12:34,987 --> 00:12:36,011
Listen up, everybody.

108
00:12:36,188 --> 00:12:39,988
We're gonna go back to the platform.
I need everybody to--

109
00:12:40,159 --> 00:12:41,387
Regina. Let's do it again.

110
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:42,857
Conduct those people.

111
00:12:44,230 --> 00:12:47,063
Listen. Now, we're gonna head back
towards the platform.

112
00:12:47,233 --> 00:12:49,064
I want everybody to slowly get up.

113
00:12:49,235 --> 00:12:51,567
-I'm gonna get you off this train.
-Good.

114
00:12:51,737 --> 00:12:55,571
Now, we're gonna be on the tracks,
so if you don't need it, leave it.

115
00:13:07,486 --> 00:13:09,078
Have been put on alert regarding--

116
00:13:09,255 --> 00:13:12,122
Right here, right here.
Right here, right here.

117
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:13,986
Cross right here, right here.

118
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:17,721
-Go.
-Cross over right here, right here.

119
00:13:17,897 --> 00:13:18,921
Let's go.

120
00:13:19,098 --> 00:13:21,396
-Up the stairs, up the stairs.
-Here you go.

121
00:13:21,567 --> 00:13:24,502
-Every cop in the city is on the way.
-Maybe it wasn't gunshots.

122
00:13:24,670 --> 00:13:27,138
Train could be blowing breakers.
Or the motor blew?

123
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:29,501
No, this is on purpose.

124
00:13:30,376 --> 00:13:31,707
Fuck you.

125
00:13:31,877 --> 00:13:34,004
-Yeah, I'm coming.
-Get the fuck off the walls.

126
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:36,239
Shut the fuck up and come on.

127
00:13:36,415 --> 00:13:38,975
Shit. Come on.

128
00:13:39,952 --> 00:13:43,683
Ramos.
Turn the power off from there down.

129
00:13:43,856 --> 00:13:44,914
What?

130
00:13:45,090 --> 00:13:47,388
Turn the power off from there down!

131
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:49,687
Okay, I got it!

132
00:13:52,431 --> 00:13:54,228
My fucking lucky day.

133
00:13:57,069 --> 00:14:00,596
Shit.
What the fuck is wrong with you, man?

134
00:14:16,255 --> 00:14:20,214
Pelham 123 to Rail Control Center.
Do you read me?

135
00:14:22,561 --> 00:14:24,256
Yes, I read you, Pelham 123.

136
00:14:24,430 --> 00:14:27,194
This is Control Center. Who is this?

137
00:14:28,267 --> 00:14:32,135
It's me, man. I didn't wanna call
till everything was ready.

138
00:14:32,304 --> 00:14:34,864
-It's not Jerry.
-I don't know who it is.

139
00:14:36,976 --> 00:14:38,773
I understand, I understand,
Pelham 123.

140
00:14:38,944 --> 00:14:40,002
Who the hell is this?

141
00:14:40,446 --> 00:14:42,414
This is the man
who's gonna rock this city.

142
00:14:42,581 --> 00:14:45,448
This is the man who's gonna
give the city a run for the money.

143
00:14:45,618 --> 00:14:48,644
Look up. Look up at your screen
and you tell me what you see.

144
00:14:48,821 --> 00:14:50,789
You see what I've done?

145
00:14:50,956 --> 00:14:51,980
I see it.

146
00:14:52,157 --> 00:14:55,183
One car is much more manageable
than 10 with the manpower I got.

147
00:14:55,361 --> 00:14:58,125
Motorman's gonna tell you
about it. Tell him what we got.

148
00:14:58,297 --> 00:14:59,958
They got hostages, lots of them.

149
00:15:00,132 --> 00:15:02,657
-And they got machine guns.
-That's Jerry.

150
00:15:02,835 --> 00:15:04,632
-That's Jerry.
-Yeah, that's right.

151
00:15:04,803 --> 00:15:06,464
Check me,
do you understand that?

152
00:15:08,007 --> 00:15:09,372
I check, I understand.

153
00:15:11,810 --> 00:15:13,334
Didn't I tell you to knock first?

154
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:17,506
Good, because this is what we call
a cash transaction.

155
00:15:17,683 --> 00:15:20,083
Now, you understand commodities,
don't you?

156
00:15:20,519 --> 00:15:23,215
You know, pork bellies?
Gold? Light crude?

157
00:15:23,389 --> 00:15:27,849
Listen, no disrespect, but maybe I'm
not the guy you should be talking to.

158
00:15:28,027 --> 00:15:30,222
Oh, no, you are exactly the guy
I wanna talk to.

159
00:15:30,396 --> 00:15:33,092
Now, I want you to look at the ticker
and you tell me...

160
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:36,666
...what is the going rate
for a New York City hostage today?

161
00:15:38,404 --> 00:15:41,567
You think a million dollars
is too much? I do. I think it's corny.

162
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:44,106
Now get your calculator out.
You got one?

163
00:15:47,813 --> 00:15:50,407
-Do you have a calculator?
-Yeah, we got one. I got one.

164
00:15:50,582 --> 00:15:56,214
Okay, good. Add this up.
You got $526,315 and 79 cents.

165
00:15:56,388 --> 00:16:00,085
That's 526,315.79.

166
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,018
Now, times that by 19.

167
00:16:03,195 --> 00:16:04,389
What do you got?

168
00:16:04,563 --> 00:16:06,827
What is he, a goddamn accountant?

169
00:16:10,202 --> 00:16:11,965
-That's 10 million?
-What do you got?

170
00:16:12,404 --> 00:16:15,100
That comes out to 10 million
plus one cent.

171
00:16:15,274 --> 00:16:16,298
That is a deal.

172
00:16:16,475 --> 00:16:18,773
You call the mayor
and you tell him the price.

173
00:16:18,944 --> 00:16:22,903
And then you tell him I want it in
100,000 $100 bills, you got that?

174
00:16:23,282 --> 00:16:24,874
I got it. What about the one cent?

175
00:16:25,050 --> 00:16:26,779
Keep that, that's your broker fee.

176
00:16:26,952 --> 00:16:29,887
Now, I want the rest
in plain suitcases...

177
00:16:30,055 --> 00:16:33,183
...the kind with the wheels
and the portable handle, okay?

178
00:16:33,359 --> 00:16:36,453
Now, this is not a futures contract.
This is a spot trade.

179
00:16:36,628 --> 00:16:39,654
That means there's a time limit on it.
Okay, you got that?

180
00:16:39,832 --> 00:16:42,062
Now, what do you think
is a fair time limit?

181
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:46,964
You know, I don't know.
I'm really just a guy--

182
00:16:47,139 --> 00:16:50,108
Come on, give me a time limit.
Give me a fair time limit.

183
00:16:52,978 --> 00:16:55,037
-Thursday.
-I was thinking more like an hour.

184
00:16:55,214 --> 00:16:56,806
Now, what's your watch say?

185
00:16:58,984 --> 00:17:00,076
Two-thirteen.

186
00:17:00,252 --> 00:17:02,015
Oh,
that's exactly what my watch says.

187
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:05,350
So at 3:13, I want that money here,
motherfucker.

188
00:17:06,091 --> 00:17:08,889
And after that, there is a late fee.

189
00:17:09,061 --> 00:17:11,495
What do you think
that late fee is gonna be?

190
00:17:14,833 --> 00:17:16,630
Come on, tell me what it'll be.

191
00:17:17,302 --> 00:17:20,169
You're gonna kill the passengers?

192
00:17:20,339 --> 00:17:22,273
Oh, commodities
is what I start to kill.

193
00:17:22,441 --> 00:17:25,274
One for every minute
past the deadline I am forced to wait.

194
00:17:25,444 --> 00:17:27,173
They become more valuable
this way...

195
00:17:27,346 --> 00:17:28,870
...and still at the same price.

196
00:17:29,314 --> 00:17:31,782
He's underground.
He's never gonna pull this off.

197
00:17:31,950 --> 00:17:34,578
-Don't tell me, tell him.
-Who the hell is this guy?

198
00:17:34,753 --> 00:17:37,221
-I don't know who it is!
-Garber, just stay with it.

199
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:38,981
What's your name?

200
00:17:39,158 --> 00:17:40,955
-What's your name, my man?
-My name?

201
00:17:41,527 --> 00:17:43,188
What's your name?

202
00:17:44,430 --> 00:17:45,692
Tell him?

203
00:17:47,132 --> 00:17:48,463
-Garber.
-Garber, okay.

204
00:17:48,634 --> 00:17:50,329
Now, seriously, man,
in 59 minutes...

205
00:17:50,502 --> 00:17:52,265
...I'm gonna start killing passengers.

206
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:55,737
So my advice to you is to get on
the phone, get the mayor notified now.

207
00:17:56,175 --> 00:17:57,608
Listen, I mean....

208
00:17:57,776 --> 00:18:00,836
I'm just a civil-service employee.
I can't get ahold of the mayor.

209
00:18:01,013 --> 00:18:02,412
That's your problem, not mine.

210
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:05,948
It's like, who's responsible for
who lives and who dies in New York?

211
00:18:06,118 --> 00:18:07,585
That's New York City's problem.

212
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:11,746
Get the fuck off the radio
and notify the mayor, motherfucker!

213
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:15,488
Okay.

214
00:18:24,570 --> 00:18:27,835
Nine months of this and I'm free.
Next mayor gets inaugurated...

215
00:18:28,006 --> 00:18:31,066
...I'm gonna be in Saint-Tropez
on the beach with a pina colada.

216
00:18:31,243 --> 00:18:33,609
I will never have to ride the subway
ever again.

217
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:36,771
-Never say never, sir.
-Never.

218
00:18:37,249 --> 00:18:39,114
All right,
what's next for the afternoon?

219
00:18:39,384 --> 00:18:40,851
East Harlem Elementary at 2:30.

220
00:18:41,019 --> 00:18:43,544
You're to read
The Cat In The Hat to the third grade.

221
00:18:43,722 --> 00:18:47,021
Every time I go to the schools,
I get sick. They all have runny noses.

222
00:18:47,192 --> 00:18:50,889
Call Dr. Katz, tell him I want him
waiting at the school, with a flu shot.

223
00:19:05,043 --> 00:19:06,738
Mayor's office.

224
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:13,550
-He's in Car 3.
-Yeah.

225
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:16,444
What happened?

226
00:19:16,889 --> 00:19:18,823
Somebody just hijacked a 6 train.

227
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:21,425
It's stopped in the tunnel
between 51st and 42nd.

228
00:19:21,593 --> 00:19:24,289
Another idiot with a gun.
What do we know?

229
00:19:24,463 --> 00:19:27,091
It's unclear, but I have a car
waiting for us downstairs.

230
00:19:27,266 --> 00:19:28,824
Subway will get us there faster.

231
00:19:29,001 --> 00:19:30,866
All right. Let the doors close.

232
00:19:31,036 --> 00:19:33,596
Tell them we'll meet them
at 59th Street.

233
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:40,744
Tell the conductor
this is now an express.

234
00:19:40,913 --> 00:19:43,074
-We're skipping the next five stops.
-What?

235
00:19:43,248 --> 00:19:45,682
-I gotta get to work.
-Hold on, hold on.

236
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:48,911
Everybody will get where they
need to go, we'll make all the stops.

237
00:19:49,087 --> 00:19:51,612
Maybe he's not such a douchebag
after all, huh?

238
00:19:52,991 --> 00:19:54,083
Funny.

239
00:19:57,529 --> 00:19:59,793
Figures you'd be the one
to get a call like this.

240
00:19:59,965 --> 00:20:03,457
Hostage negotiation team here in five
minutes and the mayor's been notified.

241
00:20:03,635 --> 00:20:05,762
-You gonna tell him?
-Get the fuck out of here.

242
00:20:05,938 --> 00:20:08,133
My shift's over in 10 minutes.

243
00:20:08,307 --> 00:20:10,036
-What are you staring at?
-Your face.

244
00:20:10,209 --> 00:20:12,370
I'm trying to remember
for when it's not here.

245
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:15,445
-You gonna start in on me?
-Right, I'm gonna start in on you.

246
00:20:15,614 --> 00:20:17,707
-Don't fuck this up, Garber.
-You wanna do it?

247
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:19,441
It's your station, your call.

248
00:20:19,618 --> 00:20:21,984
-Oh, it's my call now?
-That's right. Your call.

249
00:20:22,487 --> 00:20:23,511
Come on.

250
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:32,663
Pelham 123, come in, this is
Rail Control Center. Are you there?

251
00:20:33,098 --> 00:20:35,692
Gerber Baby boy. What's up?

252
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:40,235
Garber. Just wanted to let you know
the mayor's been notified.

253
00:20:40,672 --> 00:20:41,866
Are they gonna pay?

254
00:20:42,708 --> 00:20:45,836
I don't know. I'm just the,
what'd you call me? The broker.

255
00:20:46,011 --> 00:20:48,912
No, no, you represent
the city of New York right now, buddy.

256
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:52,642
I can tell you you're dealing with one
of the all-time bureaucracies, I know.

257
00:20:52,818 --> 00:20:55,878
-I mean, it takes time.
-You'd better fix the bureaucracy...

258
00:20:56,054 --> 00:20:58,818
...because when the time comes,
these hostages...

259
00:20:58,991 --> 00:21:01,482
...are gonna go real quick.

260
00:21:03,295 --> 00:21:05,763
You got it, you got it.
Any other demands?

261
00:21:05,931 --> 00:21:07,899
Yeah,
no fucking pizza for them, either.

262
00:21:08,066 --> 00:21:10,899
No, I mean, are you guys, like,
you know, are you terrorists?

263
00:21:11,069 --> 00:21:14,095
Do I sound like a terrorist?
Do I terrorize you?

264
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:17,572
Actually, you don't, but I mean,
not that I ever talked to one.

265
00:21:17,743 --> 00:21:18,767
So--

266
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:21,606
So, what, this is just about money?

267
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:23,407
Oh, is there anything else?

268
00:21:23,582 --> 00:21:24,844
There's not dying.

269
00:21:25,017 --> 00:21:28,418
Yeah, well, you live, you die. You
go with the current or you fight it...

270
00:21:28,587 --> 00:21:30,248
...you all end up
in the same place.

271
00:21:30,422 --> 00:21:33,391
-Where's that, Jersey?
-Yeah, you watch it. I was born there.

272
00:21:33,925 --> 00:21:36,257
I'm just saying,
you're up in the motorman's cab.

273
00:21:36,428 --> 00:21:39,864
That means you're on the radio, which
means that you're an easy target.

274
00:21:40,032 --> 00:21:42,000
You gotta know the drill.

275
00:21:43,235 --> 00:21:44,930
I know that soon I won't be alone...

276
00:21:45,103 --> 00:21:48,766
...and if I'm the first to get shot,
I'm the first of many to get shot.

277
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:51,033
That's correct,
but then you'd still be dead.

278
00:21:51,877 --> 00:21:55,108
Dead is an improvement on a lot
of things I can think of, buddy boy.

279
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:56,770
Sounds like he slept with my ex.

280
00:21:58,650 --> 00:22:00,641
You know, we all owe God a death.

281
00:22:00,819 --> 00:22:04,619
And I'm a man who pays his debts.
Are you a man who pays his debts?

282
00:22:04,790 --> 00:22:07,884
Yeah, yeah, sure.
TV, cable, and my mortgage.

283
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:12,463
-That's a little like dying once a month.
-You're married, you're a married man.

284
00:22:12,798 --> 00:22:13,822
Maybe.

285
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:18,333
No, no, no. You're married, man.
Married men have mortgages.

286
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:20,638
You got a mortgage?

287
00:22:20,806 --> 00:22:23,604
I don't know. Why don't you tell me,
then we'll both know?

288
00:22:23,775 --> 00:22:28,769
I don't know. I'm sure someone
out there loves you dearly and...

289
00:22:28,947 --> 00:22:30,778
...you know,
would be worried about you.

290
00:22:30,949 --> 00:22:32,746
You're in the motorman's cab...

291
00:22:32,918 --> 00:22:35,182
...you got no cover,
sniper on the way.

292
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:37,822
Well, you know,
circumstances are my protection...

293
00:22:37,989 --> 00:22:41,152
...because right now, you know,
hostages are good insurance.

294
00:22:41,326 --> 00:22:43,851
By the way I see it,
I'm pretty well-protected.

295
00:22:46,565 --> 00:22:49,557
You know, this reminds me
of being in a confessional.

296
00:22:50,001 --> 00:22:51,525
Are you Catholic?

297
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:53,436
I'm married, you're Catholic.

298
00:22:53,605 --> 00:22:55,664
-Maybe. I don't know.
-No, you're Catholic.

299
00:22:55,841 --> 00:22:57,035
And a good Catholic...

300
00:22:57,209 --> 00:22:59,700
...would know he's got
a trainload of innocent people.

301
00:22:59,878 --> 00:23:02,039
You don't wanna
kill innocent people, do you?

302
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:04,614
A good Catholic
knows that nobody is innocent.

303
00:23:04,783 --> 00:23:08,583
And I'm not gonna kill all these
hostages. I'd give up my leverage.

304
00:23:12,290 --> 00:23:14,952
Well,
I hope you know what you're doing.

305
00:23:15,127 --> 00:23:19,291
It's running like a fucking Swiss watch
down here, so don't worry about it.

306
00:23:21,032 --> 00:23:22,693
So, what do I call you anyway?

307
00:23:23,935 --> 00:23:24,959
Call me Ryder.

308
00:23:25,771 --> 00:23:27,068
As in "train rider"?

309
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:29,332
Call me Ryder, with a Y.

310
00:23:29,508 --> 00:23:30,634
Ryder.

311
00:23:32,844 --> 00:23:34,004
I like you, Garber.

312
00:23:34,846 --> 00:23:36,814
I do like you, man.

313
00:23:36,982 --> 00:23:38,973
You may be
the last friend I ever make.

314
00:23:40,519 --> 00:23:44,250
Well, I hope you're wrong, Mr. Ryder.
But, you know, I'm just a guy.

315
00:23:44,423 --> 00:23:46,584
I'm just a guy
on the other end of the mic.

316
00:23:47,959 --> 00:23:49,824
Oh, you don't think
this was meant to be?

317
00:23:49,995 --> 00:23:53,226
You don't think this was fate,
you and me?

318
00:23:54,132 --> 00:23:56,692
I don't know. Things happen
that lead to other things.

319
00:23:56,868 --> 00:23:59,166
And maybe this was one of them,
but that's it.

320
00:23:59,337 --> 00:24:02,932
I never get excited
about coincidence.

321
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:05,872
Well, you got 50 fucking minutes,
so check me.

322
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:08,412
All right. 50 minutes, check.

323
00:24:08,847 --> 00:24:10,712
And don't call me
unless you got news.

324
00:24:10,882 --> 00:24:13,680
-You got it.
-Motherfucker.

325
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:15,518
G.B.

326
00:24:15,954 --> 00:24:17,182
You're fucking good, man.

327
00:24:21,359 --> 00:24:23,190
Okay. Move it the other way.

328
00:24:28,066 --> 00:24:31,467
All right, come on, move it.
The other way.

329
00:24:34,973 --> 00:24:37,567
Okay, now move it back a little less.

330
00:24:41,213 --> 00:24:43,204
Bingo. Got it.

331
00:24:43,648 --> 00:24:44,876
All right, we got it.

332
00:25:19,150 --> 00:25:21,550
-Who's talked to these jokers?
-That would be me.

333
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:23,551
Yeah, under my supervision.
Who are you?

334
00:25:23,722 --> 00:25:25,986
Vincent Camonetti,
NYPD Hostage Negotiation Team.

335
00:25:26,157 --> 00:25:27,681
John Johnson,
Chief Transportation Officer.

336
00:25:29,027 --> 00:25:32,190
Walter Garber.
I'm Console Dispatch, right now.

337
00:25:32,364 --> 00:25:33,797
What can you tell me, Walter?

338
00:25:34,232 --> 00:25:36,029
His name is Ryder, with a Y.

339
00:25:36,201 --> 00:25:39,830
And he's asking
for $10 million by 3:13.

340
00:25:40,005 --> 00:25:44,135
Looking toward the future. Say what
he'd do if he doesn't get the money?

341
00:25:44,309 --> 00:25:46,869
He said he'd kill a passenger
every minute we go over.

342
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:49,411
-Starting at 3:13 p.m.?
-3-1-3, yes, sir.

343
00:25:49,581 --> 00:25:51,378
-Anything else?
-He's smart.

344
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:54,280
If he's smart, why is he doing
something so fucking stupid?

345
00:25:54,452 --> 00:25:56,682
-On the train radio?
-We can get him right here.

346
00:25:56,855 --> 00:25:59,016
Any chance that we can get
a signal down there?

347
00:25:59,190 --> 00:26:01,055
We'd like to get him
on one of our cells.

348
00:26:01,226 --> 00:26:03,160
No,
there's no chance, not where he is.

349
00:26:04,195 --> 00:26:06,493
What's this?
"Leverage, spot trade"?

350
00:26:06,665 --> 00:26:09,532
Yeah, it's weird. He's like
a money guy, like a Wall Street.

351
00:26:09,701 --> 00:26:13,432
He talked about the passengers
like they were commodities.

352
00:26:13,605 --> 00:26:15,698
-"Catholic"?
-Yeah, I think he's Catholic.

353
00:26:15,874 --> 00:26:19,401
For chrissakes, Garber, you gonna tell
us what his zodiac sign is now?

354
00:26:19,578 --> 00:26:21,478
I'm just saying I think he's Catholic.

355
00:26:21,646 --> 00:26:24,911
Man asked me about "Catholic."
I wrote it down. I'm giving my opinion.

356
00:26:25,083 --> 00:26:26,846
Unlike other people,
I have an opinion.

357
00:26:27,018 --> 00:26:29,248
Fellas, can we settle
this dispute later?

358
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:31,480
-Absolutely.
-Why do you think he's Catholic?

359
00:26:31,656 --> 00:26:35,114
I think he's Catholic because he talked
about original sin and confessions.

360
00:26:35,293 --> 00:26:37,557
I wrote it down.
I didn't know what else to do.

361
00:26:37,729 --> 00:26:39,390
-Did he ask for a priest?
-No.

362
00:26:39,564 --> 00:26:41,225
Good. Anything else?

363
00:26:43,001 --> 00:26:47,097
He sounded, the way he was talking,
he sounded like he's not afraid to die.

364
00:26:48,139 --> 00:26:49,401
Yeah, well, it's early yet.

365
00:26:50,775 --> 00:26:52,868
-The calls are coming through...?
-Right here.

366
00:26:53,044 --> 00:26:55,012
You hit the blue button,
you can reach him.

367
00:26:55,180 --> 00:26:57,512
-He'll come back to you.
-Mind if I take your seat?

368
00:26:57,682 --> 00:27:00,082
-No, no, go right ahead.
-Thank you, Walter.

369
00:27:00,251 --> 00:27:01,275
You're welcome.

370
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:04,217
This is the six wire.
You don't have to touch that one.

371
00:27:04,389 --> 00:27:05,913
-Okay.
-That goes around the room.

372
00:27:06,091 --> 00:27:07,319
-Six wire.
-Why don't you--

373
00:27:07,492 --> 00:27:09,585
Just hit the talk here
and then that mutes it.

374
00:27:09,761 --> 00:27:11,854
Take the rest of the day off.
Get out of here.

375
00:27:12,030 --> 00:27:14,555
I thought I'd stick around,
just make sure that....

376
00:27:14,733 --> 00:27:19,193
Well, that wasn't a suggestion.
So why don't you go home?

377
00:27:22,273 --> 00:27:23,638
All right.

378
00:27:24,976 --> 00:27:27,911
This is it. You got all the information
over here about the 313.

379
00:27:28,079 --> 00:27:30,946
-Wait for his call.
-You want me to work it up right now?

380
00:27:31,116 --> 00:27:34,608
You call headquarters, let them know
that I'm here and I'm on the job. Okay.

381
00:27:48,233 --> 00:27:49,928
I gotta take a piss.

382
00:27:50,101 --> 00:27:51,329
So who's stopping you?

383
00:27:51,503 --> 00:27:56,304
All right. We wouldn't wanna end up
on any Amnesty lnternational lists...

384
00:27:56,474 --> 00:27:59,034
...so step up to the door, face out.

385
00:27:59,210 --> 00:28:01,110
Open the middle door.

386
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:03,677
Do what you gotta do.

387
00:28:06,084 --> 00:28:07,779
Can I jump down there?

388
00:28:20,231 --> 00:28:22,597
-You gotta go or don't you?
-I do, I gotta go.

389
00:28:23,802 --> 00:28:26,965
Step up, my man. Let's go, let's go.

390
00:28:36,781 --> 00:28:39,579
That kid's going places.
All right, close the doors.

391
00:28:39,751 --> 00:28:41,116
Pelham 123, come in.

392
00:28:41,286 --> 00:28:44,983
-Pelham 123, please come in.
-All right, everybody, sit down!

393
00:28:56,267 --> 00:28:57,291
Who is this?

394
00:28:57,469 --> 00:29:01,405
This is Lieutenant Camonetti. I'm with
the NYPD Hostage Negotiation Team.

395
00:29:01,573 --> 00:29:04,235
I'd like to talk to you
about the situation that we're in.

396
00:29:04,409 --> 00:29:05,899
Where the fuck is Garber?

397
00:29:06,077 --> 00:29:07,635
Mr. Garber is a train dispatcher.

398
00:29:07,812 --> 00:29:10,872
-This is now a police matter.
-Yeah, well, I wanna talk to Garber.

399
00:29:11,049 --> 00:29:15,076
I'm sorry, Mr. Ryder,
but Mr. Garber is no longer involved.

400
00:29:16,321 --> 00:29:17,811
Motorman, up!

401
00:29:19,390 --> 00:29:21,085
-Put Garber on.
-To be honest...

402
00:29:21,259 --> 00:29:22,817
...Mr. Garber has gone home.

403
00:29:22,994 --> 00:29:25,485
Put Garber on the fucking line
or I kill the motorman.

404
00:29:27,398 --> 00:29:31,459
I guarantee you I am the best person
for you to be talking to right now.

405
00:29:31,636 --> 00:29:33,365
Give me a moment
and I'll explain why.

406
00:29:33,905 --> 00:29:36,533
You were always
gonna be the first one to go.

407
00:29:36,975 --> 00:29:38,067
Oh, Jesus!

408
00:29:38,943 --> 00:29:40,604
Jesus.

409
00:29:44,249 --> 00:29:45,273
Mr. Camonetti...

410
00:29:45,450 --> 00:29:48,283
...you got 60 fucking seconds
before I kill another.

411
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:52,082
-Okay? Fifty-nine, 58, 57....
-Get him. Just get Garber.

412
00:29:52,257 --> 00:29:54,885
-Fifty-six, 55, 54....
-We're trying to locate Garber...

413
00:29:55,059 --> 00:29:57,050
...ASAP, Mr. Ryder.
Why did you do that?

414
00:29:57,228 --> 00:30:00,789
Mr. Camonetti or whatever
fucking greaseball name you got...

415
00:30:00,965 --> 00:30:03,365
...the city of fucking New York
killed Jerry, okay?

416
00:30:03,535 --> 00:30:06,732
Fifty-three, 52, 51....

417
00:30:10,475 --> 00:30:11,703
Garber. Garber!

418
00:30:11,876 --> 00:30:15,334
Garber, he killed Jerry Pollard, man.

419
00:30:15,513 --> 00:30:18,107
Come on,
he wants to talk to you right now.

420
00:30:19,551 --> 00:30:20,950
He's here. He's on the way.

421
00:30:22,220 --> 00:30:26,589
Eleven, 10, nine, eight, seven....

422
00:30:26,758 --> 00:30:32,492
-He's approaching the desk.
-Six, five, four, three, two, one....

423
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:34,131
Hey, it's me, it's Garber.

424
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:36,831
Garber! You didn't say goodbye.

425
00:30:38,770 --> 00:30:39,794
You killed Jerry?

426
00:30:39,971 --> 00:30:43,065
No, the city of fucking New York
killed Jerry, okay?

427
00:30:43,241 --> 00:30:47,234
The biggest rathole
in the world fucking killed Jerry.

428
00:30:47,412 --> 00:30:50,313
Okay? Now you can
chalk another victim up to NYC.

429
00:30:50,481 --> 00:30:53,609
-Now, can everybody hear me?
-Yeah, we hear you, loud and clear.

430
00:30:53,785 --> 00:30:55,582
Now you don't have to tell
the cops...

431
00:30:55,753 --> 00:30:59,746
...they don't tell me how to do it or how
it's gonna be. I fucking tell them.

432
00:30:59,924 --> 00:31:01,721
Don't you ever, ever
leave me again.

433
00:31:01,893 --> 00:31:04,555
Or I'll just have to hunt you down
and I'll kill you.

434
00:31:04,729 --> 00:31:07,357
Now, you got 39--

435
00:31:07,966 --> 00:31:10,457
Thirty-nine minutes. Check me.

436
00:31:11,302 --> 00:31:12,428
Thirty-nine, check.

437
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:24,805
This is Staley to ESU 2.
What's your position?

438
00:31:24,983 --> 00:31:27,474
ESU 2 approaching hostage car
from south tunnel.

439
00:31:27,919 --> 00:31:29,181
Go, go, go.

440
00:31:31,289 --> 00:31:34,315
Ten-million dollars. I'll write him
a check and get it over with.

441
00:31:34,492 --> 00:31:37,893
-He wants it in cash.
-I was joking, LaSalle.

442
00:31:38,529 --> 00:31:41,123
But we've been given one hour
to get the money together.

443
00:31:41,299 --> 00:31:43,733
Ten-million dollars.
Where do they get these numbers?

444
00:31:43,902 --> 00:31:46,063
Actually, 10 is the limit, sir.

445
00:31:46,237 --> 00:31:47,261
Why is that?

446
00:31:47,438 --> 00:31:50,703
Request to the City Controller,
he forwards it to one of our lenders...

447
00:31:50,875 --> 00:31:54,902
...cash gets released to the Federal
Reserve. Limit at any time is 10 million.

448
00:31:55,079 --> 00:31:57,741
Some idiot with a gun
wouldn't know that. I didn't know.

449
00:31:57,916 --> 00:32:00,749
-Well, you're very busy, sir.
-How do you know that?

450
00:32:02,253 --> 00:32:03,845
Here he is.

451
00:32:04,055 --> 00:32:06,990
-Henry, what's the situation?
-They killed a hostage.

452
00:32:07,158 --> 00:32:09,183
These guys may be the real deal.

453
00:32:09,360 --> 00:32:11,351
I thought there was one idiot
with a gun.

454
00:32:11,529 --> 00:32:14,225
Multiple gunmen. They're not sure.
They've got 18 hostages.

455
00:32:14,399 --> 00:32:17,630
They'll kill more in an hour. That's
the limit. They want you to know.

456
00:32:17,802 --> 00:32:19,326
-What do we know?
-Not amateurs.

457
00:32:19,504 --> 00:32:21,233
They cut out a car,
stopped on a rise.

458
00:32:21,406 --> 00:32:23,431
They can see us coming
100 yards either way.

459
00:32:23,608 --> 00:32:25,075
How long to get the money?

460
00:32:25,243 --> 00:32:26,403
-I don't know.
-Find out.

461
00:32:26,577 --> 00:32:30,172
-You're not thinking of paying, are you?
-I'm thinking of time and being ready.

462
00:32:30,348 --> 00:32:32,339
Call the Controller.
Tell them we'll pay.

463
00:32:34,752 --> 00:32:37,118
What's with you and Garber, huh?
Tell me about him.

464
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:38,414
Scheduled to work today?

465
00:32:38,589 --> 00:32:40,784
-Yeah, absolutely. But....
-But what?

466
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:43,792
He's only had this particular job
for a couple weeks now.

467
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:46,590
-Well, why is that?
-Well, he's under investigation.

468
00:32:46,764 --> 00:32:48,026
What?

469
00:32:48,199 --> 00:32:51,191
-We were gonna suspend him--
-What's he being investigated for?

470
00:32:54,405 --> 00:32:57,203
He went to Japan. He had to take
a look at some new trains...

471
00:32:57,375 --> 00:32:59,468
...and the allegation
is that he took a bribe.

472
00:32:59,644 --> 00:33:01,305
Took a bribe?
Does he have a record?

473
00:33:01,479 --> 00:33:02,878
-Not that I know.
-You sure?

474
00:33:03,047 --> 00:33:05,481
Yeah, yeah. I don't think so.
I gotta take this.

475
00:33:05,683 --> 00:33:08,880
The identity of the hijackers
is still unclear.

476
00:33:09,053 --> 00:33:13,149
The Hostage Negotiation Team has
just arrived at MTA headquarters...

477
00:33:13,324 --> 00:33:16,259
... to determine
if this is a terrorist enterprise.

478
00:33:16,961 --> 00:33:19,794
Is that what we are? An enterprise?

479
00:33:21,566 --> 00:33:22,794
We're an enterprise.

480
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:31,207
Well, pilot reports
that the aircraft has begun its descent.

481
00:33:37,482 --> 00:33:40,315
This is Staley to ESU 4.
What's your ETA?

482
00:33:40,485 --> 00:33:43,249
Approximately two minutes
south of target.

483
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:46,016
Why is the train called
Pelham 123?

484
00:33:46,624 --> 00:33:49,149
Comes out of Pelham Bay
at 1:23 in the afternoon.

485
00:33:49,927 --> 00:33:52,157
How did you end up with this call?

486
00:33:52,330 --> 00:33:54,264
It's a Lexington Avenue train.

487
00:33:54,432 --> 00:33:56,923
I got the Lexington Avenue desk.
Came through my desk.

488
00:33:57,101 --> 00:33:59,296
Can you think of a reason
why you'd be targeted?

489
00:33:59,470 --> 00:34:02,496
Someone wanna hurt you?
Something against you or something?

490
00:34:02,673 --> 00:34:03,901
No.

491
00:34:10,448 --> 00:34:12,040
You recognize his voice?

492
00:34:13,618 --> 00:34:17,611
No. No, as I said, it was a coincidence
it came through my desk.

493
00:34:19,023 --> 00:34:22,356
Did you pick this desk?
Or was it assigned to you?

494
00:34:23,995 --> 00:34:25,360
Did l...?

495
00:34:25,530 --> 00:34:28,499
I said, did you pick this desk
or was it assigned to you?

496
00:34:34,839 --> 00:34:36,238
Can I take my coat off?

497
00:34:39,811 --> 00:34:41,005
Doesn't make any sense.

498
00:34:41,179 --> 00:34:42,908
-What doesn't?
-Guy you're talking to.

499
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:46,414
He ain't a train dispatcher.
Walter Garber.

500
00:34:46,584 --> 00:34:48,575
-He's a big shot.
-Big shot at what?

501
00:34:48,753 --> 00:34:50,914
Rail Control.
I mean, he runs things up there.

502
00:34:51,089 --> 00:34:53,751
-At least he did before I went up.
-His name is Walter?

503
00:34:53,925 --> 00:34:55,256
Yeah.

504
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:59,563
Dude like that
shouldn't be answering the phone.

505
00:35:05,103 --> 00:35:07,867
-Mr. Ryder wants to talk to you.
-Right.

506
00:35:08,039 --> 00:35:10,940
Are you sure you don't have
some sort of relationship with him?

507
00:35:11,109 --> 00:35:15,546
I assure you, whatever relationship
I have with him is better than yours.

508
00:35:15,713 --> 00:35:18,614
Jerry, my friend, was killed
while you were talking to Ryder.

509
00:35:18,783 --> 00:35:21,308
Maybe that's a question
you ask yourself instead of me.

510
00:35:21,486 --> 00:35:23,420
I didn't have anything to do
with this.

511
00:35:23,588 --> 00:35:26,284
But what I have in you,
Mr. Garber, is an unknown variable.

512
00:35:26,457 --> 00:35:28,982
-Unknown variable?
-Right. People's lives are at stake.

513
00:35:29,160 --> 00:35:30,627
-I understand that.
-Excuse me...

514
00:35:30,795 --> 00:35:33,127
...if I try to get more comfortable
with you, okay?

515
00:35:33,931 --> 00:35:36,024
It ain't working, but okay.

516
00:35:36,834 --> 00:35:38,165
Now, with that in mind...

517
00:35:38,336 --> 00:35:41,897
...would you agree
to a consensual search of your house?

518
00:35:42,073 --> 00:35:44,064
Take me 40, 45 minutes
to get a warrant.

519
00:35:46,010 --> 00:35:47,568
What....

520
00:35:49,714 --> 00:35:50,976
Yes, okay.

521
00:35:54,719 --> 00:35:56,050
Got him.

522
00:35:56,854 --> 00:35:59,254
Walter Garber, right there.

523
00:35:59,757 --> 00:36:01,884
No shit, look at this.

524
00:36:05,596 --> 00:36:08,565
-Guy took a bribe, man.
-Yeah.

525
00:36:09,734 --> 00:36:10,758
Baby!

526
00:36:21,312 --> 00:36:23,974
ESU 2, this is Staley.
What's your overall status?

527
00:36:24,148 --> 00:36:25,615
All positions secured.

528
00:36:25,783 --> 00:36:28,308
All right,
hold your fire until instructed.

529
00:36:34,926 --> 00:36:37,087
Pelham 123, can you hear me?

530
00:36:37,528 --> 00:36:39,359
Yeah, loud and clear, back at you.

531
00:36:39,530 --> 00:36:41,998
All right,
the mayor has agreed to pay...

532
00:36:42,166 --> 00:36:44,600
...and they're getting the money
together right now.

533
00:36:44,769 --> 00:36:45,793
Good.

534
00:36:45,970 --> 00:36:49,633
Well, you know, you got 28 minutes,
so I advise him to make haste.

535
00:36:50,074 --> 00:36:52,804
-I'm sure he will.
-So is your first name Walter?

536
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:56,036
-Excuse me?
-Your name, is it Walter?

537
00:36:58,583 --> 00:36:59,845
-Yes, it is.
-Good.

538
00:37:00,017 --> 00:37:01,814
What are you doing
dispatching trains?

539
00:37:01,986 --> 00:37:04,784
I thought you were some sort of
MTA big shot.

540
00:37:05,089 --> 00:37:08,889
I work for the MTA.
Today they put me at dispatch...

541
00:37:10,194 --> 00:37:11,218
...and my bad luck.

542
00:37:11,395 --> 00:37:13,386
I thought you didn't
believe in bad luck.

543
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:15,930
I said I didn't believe in fate.

544
00:37:16,100 --> 00:37:18,830
Do you believe in
rigged contracts for new trains?

545
00:37:20,304 --> 00:37:23,296
Look, what are
we talking about this for?

546
00:37:23,474 --> 00:37:26,375
-I need to know who I'm dealing with.
-You need to know who--?

547
00:37:26,544 --> 00:37:30,640
Yeah, I want to know who I'm dealing
with. I mean, are you a bad penny?

548
00:37:30,848 --> 00:37:32,315
Let me explain something to you.

549
00:37:33,284 --> 00:37:35,252
Being accused of something
is one thing.

550
00:37:35,419 --> 00:37:38,047
Being guilty of it
is something entirely different.

551
00:37:38,222 --> 00:37:41,623
Well, agreed. But you gotta
take me through this, my man.

552
00:37:41,792 --> 00:37:45,558
You got to tell me from the top.
This whole train thing. Come on.

553
00:37:49,800 --> 00:37:51,893
All right,
I started out in maintenance.

554
00:37:52,069 --> 00:37:55,266
Platform maintenance,
track maintenance, flagman...

555
00:37:55,973 --> 00:37:57,736
-...conductor.
-Conductor, really?

556
00:37:58,643 --> 00:38:00,543
Yeah. And then motorman.

557
00:38:00,711 --> 00:38:02,702
A motorman.
How long did you do that for?

558
00:38:03,381 --> 00:38:04,780
I drove them over six years.

559
00:38:04,949 --> 00:38:07,941
I went to tower operations,
assistant dispatcher, dispatcher.

560
00:38:08,119 --> 00:38:09,143
I finally ended up--

561
00:38:09,320 --> 00:38:12,983
Yeah, you're assistant chief
transportation officer or something.

562
00:38:13,157 --> 00:38:16,558
-Right?
-That's right.

563
00:38:17,194 --> 00:38:21,130
And part of my job is to go out
to the manufacturers, you know...

564
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:25,861
...the people who build the trains
and bid on contracts for the trains.

565
00:38:26,037 --> 00:38:27,561
Is that where you took the bribe?

566
00:38:27,738 --> 00:38:30,502
The Japanese train
over the Canadian train?

567
00:38:30,675 --> 00:38:34,873
I did not take a bribe, all right?
I was accused of taking a bribe.

568
00:38:35,046 --> 00:38:37,514
I have not been proven guilty yet.

569
00:38:37,682 --> 00:38:40,082
They haven't said yet.
I mean, they haven't decided.

570
00:38:40,251 --> 00:38:44,654
Well, they got no proof. I don't care
what they decide. It doesn't matter--

571
00:38:44,822 --> 00:38:46,483
Then is this
when they demoted you?

572
00:38:46,657 --> 00:38:49,649
That's correct. They demoted me,
pending the outcome.

573
00:38:49,827 --> 00:38:52,591
And now they're trying
to humiliate you, is that right?

574
00:38:52,763 --> 00:38:54,424
Motherfuckers.

575
00:38:54,598 --> 00:38:56,691
Look, I know
how these things work, man, okay?

576
00:38:56,867 --> 00:38:59,131
Everything doesn't seem
to appear like what it is.

577
00:38:59,303 --> 00:39:01,635
But you've gotta be
completely honest with me, man.

578
00:39:01,806 --> 00:39:04,502
-Don't know what you're talking about.
-How did you do it?

579
00:39:04,675 --> 00:39:06,836
I didn't. I'm innocent.

580
00:39:07,011 --> 00:39:08,035
Oh, you're innocent.

581
00:39:08,212 --> 00:39:10,077
No, you're talking to a Catholic,
man.

582
00:39:10,247 --> 00:39:12,943
We've been over innocent before.
Okay?

583
00:39:13,117 --> 00:39:17,315
Look, I've been through all this, man.
So just tell me, how did you do it?

584
00:39:19,724 --> 00:39:22,124
I didn't do it.

585
00:39:22,293 --> 00:39:24,352
Okay, that's it! That's fucking it!

586
00:39:24,528 --> 00:39:25,196
Damn it.

587
00:39:26,931 --> 00:39:29,195
-Kid. You.
-Me?

588
00:39:29,367 --> 00:39:32,131
No, no, you. Up.
Get the fuck over there.

589
00:39:32,636 --> 00:39:34,695
I don't know what you did
to piss him off.

590
00:39:34,872 --> 00:39:37,432
Garber.
You know what I'm looking at?

591
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:40,366
-Do you know what I'm looking at?
-No, I do not.

592
00:39:40,544 --> 00:39:43,809
First there's my gun, and at the end
of my gun-- What's your name?

593
00:39:43,981 --> 00:39:47,041
-George. Everyone calls me Geo.
-George. His friends call him Geo.

594
00:39:47,218 --> 00:39:48,981
Got this '80s skateboard thing
going.

595
00:39:49,153 --> 00:39:52,589
He makes it work, but it's not gonna
look too good in his casket.

596
00:39:53,023 --> 00:39:55,958
Listen, Ryder, just slow down.
We haven't reached the deadline.

597
00:39:56,127 --> 00:39:58,152
No, there's no fucking deadline,
man.

598
00:39:58,329 --> 00:39:59,887
You just gotta tell me the truth.

599
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:01,861
-About what?
-The bribe!

600
00:40:02,032 --> 00:40:04,296
-Did you take it?
-I didn't take a bribe.

601
00:40:04,468 --> 00:40:06,993
Okay, you got five seconds
to save this kid's life.

602
00:40:07,171 --> 00:40:08,968
I didn't do anything.

603
00:40:09,140 --> 00:40:10,869
-Five....
-Just wait a second.

604
00:40:11,041 --> 00:40:13,305
-Four, three....
-Wait a second!

605
00:40:13,477 --> 00:40:15,035
Two....

606
00:40:15,212 --> 00:40:17,976
-Fucking tell him how you did it.
-All right, okay.

607
00:40:22,853 --> 00:40:25,151
-Say it.
-I took the bribe.

608
00:40:27,024 --> 00:40:28,582
How much?

609
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:30,591
Thirty....

610
00:40:30,761 --> 00:40:32,251
How fucking much?

611
00:40:33,397 --> 00:40:35,422
Thirty-five thousand dollars.

612
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:36,998
How did you do it?

613
00:40:37,601 --> 00:40:40,536
I went to Japan
to look at these trains.

614
00:40:40,704 --> 00:40:42,433
It's part of my job.

615
00:40:42,606 --> 00:40:44,039
I....

616
00:40:44,208 --> 00:40:48,144
I don't get to vote, okay?
I just recommend.

617
00:40:48,312 --> 00:40:52,510
I chose what I thought
was the best train...

618
00:40:52,683 --> 00:40:55,675
...the Japanese had the best train,
and I made my recommendation.

619
00:40:55,853 --> 00:40:57,514
That's before you took the bribe.

620
00:40:58,155 --> 00:40:59,747
Yes.

621
00:40:59,924 --> 00:41:02,256
That was the train
you were gonna pick anyway, huh?

622
00:41:02,426 --> 00:41:05,361
-Yes.
-And now you're fighting for your job...

623
00:41:05,529 --> 00:41:07,429
...and they're trying
to humiliate you?

624
00:41:07,598 --> 00:41:11,864
No, no, no. I did what I did.

625
00:41:12,036 --> 00:41:13,867
And....

626
00:41:14,238 --> 00:41:16,866
And it's not, you know,
it's not the MTA's fault.

627
00:41:17,041 --> 00:41:18,565
What did you spend it on?

628
00:41:19,610 --> 00:41:21,874
Look, what does this
got to do with anything, huh?

629
00:41:22,046 --> 00:41:23,604
What did you fucking spend it on?

630
00:41:23,781 --> 00:41:26,909
I used the money for my kids,
all right?

631
00:41:27,084 --> 00:41:28,745
To pay my children's tuition.

632
00:41:28,919 --> 00:41:33,083
I have a 17-year-old.
I have a 19-year-old daughter.

633
00:41:33,657 --> 00:41:37,889
And I used the money to pay
for their college tuition, all right?

634
00:41:44,635 --> 00:41:45,932
You know what, Garber?

635
00:41:46,504 --> 00:41:48,267
You're my goddamn hero,
you know that?

636
00:41:48,439 --> 00:41:51,966
You got a kid here, you don't even
know him, you saved his life.

637
00:41:52,309 --> 00:41:55,972
That's brave, man.
That's fucking heroic.

638
00:41:57,047 --> 00:41:59,811
-Tell Garber thank you.
-Thank you, Garber.

639
00:41:59,984 --> 00:42:01,952
"Thank you, Garber,
for saving my life."

640
00:42:02,386 --> 00:42:04,115
Thank you, Garber,
for saving my life.

641
00:42:07,091 --> 00:42:08,752
You're welcome.

642
00:42:12,096 --> 00:42:13,586
Sit down.

643
00:42:14,398 --> 00:42:17,094
You're just like me, Garber.
I fueled this city.

644
00:42:17,268 --> 00:42:20,760
I fed it breakfast every morning,
and now we're the bad guys.

645
00:42:20,938 --> 00:42:23,873
I don't think so.
I don't fucking think so!

646
00:42:40,024 --> 00:42:42,458
-Hello, Therese.
-Honey, look.

647
00:42:42,626 --> 00:42:45,493
There are police here, Walt.
They wanna search the house.

648
00:42:45,663 --> 00:42:47,392
They said you said it was okay.

649
00:42:51,168 --> 00:42:53,568
Yeah. Yeah, it's okay.
It's-- Just let them in.

650
00:42:54,638 --> 00:42:55,696
We got nothing to hide.

651
00:42:56,140 --> 00:42:57,664
Is this about the investigation?

652
00:42:58,342 --> 00:43:00,503
No, no. You watching TV?

653
00:43:00,878 --> 00:43:03,073
This hostage thing.
Yeah, yeah, I'm watching it.

654
00:43:03,614 --> 00:43:05,639
Well, it's just that....

655
00:43:05,849 --> 00:43:07,714
I'll tell you about it
when I get home...

656
00:43:07,885 --> 00:43:11,377
...but I'm in the middle of it now and
they wanna do background checks...

657
00:43:11,555 --> 00:43:13,546
...on everybody involved here
from the MTA.

658
00:43:13,724 --> 00:43:17,285
-That's why they're at the house.
-All right, okay. But you're okay?

659
00:43:17,461 --> 00:43:20,589
I'm fine, I'm fine. Just let them in.
I'll see you when I get home.

660
00:43:20,764 --> 00:43:23,255
All right. Okay, bye.

661
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:24,560
I'm sorry, Walter.

662
00:43:25,536 --> 00:43:26,969
I am.

663
00:43:27,137 --> 00:43:30,334
Listen, don't let this guy
bring you into his reality, all right?

664
00:43:30,507 --> 00:43:33,271
That's what he wants to do.
He hurts you, you get angry.

665
00:43:33,444 --> 00:43:35,639
-He's got the advantage. Understand?
-Yeah.

666
00:43:35,813 --> 00:43:37,838
Just deflect, if you can.

667
00:43:38,682 --> 00:43:40,877
-Okay? All right.
-All right.

668
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:09,272
I hope they don't get fucking lost.

669
00:44:15,552 --> 00:44:17,383
Fuck me! Ten-million bucks.

670
00:44:19,990 --> 00:44:22,220
The joke is,
say we dipped in, took some?

671
00:44:22,393 --> 00:44:25,328
Bad guys would count it,
come up short, probably kill us.

672
00:44:25,763 --> 00:44:27,060
No shit.

673
00:44:38,676 --> 00:44:40,303
Geo, what the fuck's happening?

674
00:44:43,080 --> 00:44:46,208
Geo. Geo, what's going on?

675
00:44:48,552 --> 00:44:50,179
Geo.

676
00:44:51,789 --> 00:44:53,916
I'm a fucking hostage.

677
00:44:56,160 --> 00:45:00,392
Listen to me.
Stream it on our site. Call the news.

678
00:45:00,831 --> 00:45:02,458
Shit.

679
00:45:08,439 --> 00:45:09,872
Hey.

680
00:45:13,977 --> 00:45:17,310
We've gotta do something.
They're gonna kill us.

681
00:45:21,018 --> 00:45:22,110
You got a plan?

682
00:45:22,820 --> 00:45:24,185
I thought you'd have one.

683
00:45:31,462 --> 00:45:33,362
Because I'm some
tough-looking black guy?

684
00:45:34,465 --> 00:45:37,025
I saw that ring on your finger.

685
00:45:42,840 --> 00:45:44,330
That was a long time ago.

686
00:45:44,508 --> 00:45:47,136
-Okay?
-My husband had one just like it.

687
00:45:54,051 --> 00:45:55,382
A severe sell-off underway...

688
00:45:55,552 --> 00:45:58,817
...the Dow is down 450 points
in very heavy trading...

689
00:45:58,989 --> 00:46:01,321
...as Wall Street reacts
to the terrorist attack...

690
00:46:01,492 --> 00:46:04,427
...of the New York City
subway system.

691
00:46:11,301 --> 00:46:14,668
-How's my hair look?
-Fine. You ready to make a statement?

692
00:46:14,838 --> 00:46:16,863
When I have something to tell them.

693
00:46:17,040 --> 00:46:18,667
It's a leadership moment, sir.

694
00:46:18,842 --> 00:46:21,675
I'm not running for re-election,
for fucking president.

695
00:46:21,845 --> 00:46:24,075
I left my Rudy Giuliani suit at home.

696
00:46:24,248 --> 00:46:27,581
You're being selfish.
It'll take 30 seconds to reassure them.

697
00:46:35,058 --> 00:46:36,116
-Over there!
-Mr. Mayor!

698
00:46:36,293 --> 00:46:39,558
-Mr. Mayor! Mr. Mayor!
-Will you be making a statement?

699
00:46:39,730 --> 00:46:42,756
We're doing everything
the situation demands.

700
00:46:42,933 --> 00:46:45,800
I'm not gonna speculate right now.
All right?

701
00:46:45,969 --> 00:46:48,130
-Mayor, is it terrorism?
-No.

702
00:46:48,572 --> 00:46:50,164
Hey.

703
00:46:50,340 --> 00:46:52,240
Mayor! Are they terrorists?

704
00:46:52,409 --> 00:46:54,707
All right, all right, all right!

705
00:46:54,878 --> 00:46:57,005
Listen, nobody said anything
about terrorism...

706
00:46:57,181 --> 00:47:00,480
...or a bomb, anything like that.
Let's stop that right now, all right?

707
00:47:00,651 --> 00:47:03,415
How about your divorce? Care
to speculate how that's going?

708
00:47:03,587 --> 00:47:04,713
Your divorce, sir.

709
00:47:04,888 --> 00:47:06,788
Been a lot of talk in the news
lately...

