-Tell him it's there.

942
01:00:40,167 --> 01:00:42,192
-Four, three....
-Tell him it's here.

943
01:00:42,370 --> 01:00:43,860
-It's here.
-Two, one.

944
01:00:44,038 --> 01:00:46,632
The money's there,
it's at 42nd and Vanderbilt.

945
01:00:49,944 --> 01:00:52,936
Liar! Motherfucking liar!

946
01:00:53,114 --> 01:00:54,342
Seven.

947
01:00:55,283 --> 01:00:58,719
-One, two, three, four, five, six, seven.
-Ryder. All right, listen.

948
01:00:58,886 --> 01:01:00,615
-Lucky lady, up.
-We made a mistake.

949
01:01:00,788 --> 01:01:03,120
-I think that's him. That's Ryder.
-Lucky lady, up.

950
01:01:03,291 --> 01:01:05,691
-Listen to me, it was an accident.
-Keep talking.

951
01:01:05,860 --> 01:01:07,851
Ryder, we made a mistake.
It's my fault.

952
01:01:08,029 --> 01:01:09,758
-The car crashed.
-Tell him something!

953
01:01:09,931 --> 01:01:11,796
-That's why the money's not there.
-Up!

954
01:01:13,301 --> 01:01:14,325
-Up!
-Wait.

955
01:01:14,702 --> 01:01:16,363
-Fuck, no.
-Get up!

956
01:01:16,537 --> 01:01:17,970
Get back in line!

957
01:01:18,139 --> 01:01:19,970
Ryder, like one minute
it's gonna take.

958
01:01:24,979 --> 01:01:27,311
Don't do this, for God's sake.
It was an accident.

959
01:01:27,481 --> 01:01:28,675
-Come on.
-Wait.

960
01:01:28,849 --> 01:01:30,077
It's the only plan I got.

961
01:01:30,251 --> 01:01:31,843
Ryder, listen, it was an accident.

962
01:01:32,019 --> 01:01:34,988
It was an accident, Ryder.
We made a mistake.

963
01:01:35,156 --> 01:01:37,647
It was an accident, Ryder!
It was an accident!

964
01:01:37,825 --> 01:01:39,258
Come on, motherfucker!

965
01:01:39,994 --> 01:01:41,518
Oh, shit.

966
01:01:43,230 --> 01:01:44,424
God!

967
01:01:45,433 --> 01:01:46,764
Oh, my God.

968
01:01:52,873 --> 01:01:56,070
ESU Team 1 to Sniper 1,
do you have a shot?

969
01:01:56,243 --> 01:01:58,234
That's your fault.

970
01:02:04,552 --> 01:02:06,315
I got an easy shot. Please advise.

971
01:02:07,254 --> 01:02:09,119
-Stand by.
-Roger that.

972
01:02:21,035 --> 01:02:22,229
Shit!

973
01:02:39,420 --> 01:02:40,648
What the fuck happened?

974
01:02:42,023 --> 01:02:45,151
Accidental discharge.
I just got bit by a fucking rat.

975
01:02:45,593 --> 01:02:46,787
It's accidental discharge.

976
01:02:46,961 --> 01:02:49,327
Who? Who got shot? Was it Ryder?

977
01:02:49,497 --> 01:02:50,759
No, it was Ramos.

978
01:02:59,740 --> 01:03:02,800
-Sergeant? The money there yet?
-What? Yes, yes.

979
01:03:04,211 --> 01:03:05,610
-Are you there?
-Get in here.

980
01:03:05,780 --> 01:03:08,010
Shoot any motherfucker that moves.

981
01:03:08,683 --> 01:03:10,446
-That's an order!
-Shit on your orders.

982
01:03:10,618 --> 01:03:11,744
Can you hear me, Ryder?

983
01:03:11,919 --> 01:03:15,616
Okay,
now somebody else has to die.

984
01:03:15,790 --> 01:03:17,121
Two people, maybe all of us.

985
01:03:20,995 --> 01:03:22,019
Did you hear me?

986
01:03:22,196 --> 01:03:24,892
I heard you, but you gotta understand,
the circumstances...

987
01:03:25,066 --> 01:03:26,693
...they're different now for you.

988
01:03:26,867 --> 01:03:27,959
-You gotta rethink.
-No.

989
01:03:28,135 --> 01:03:29,295
You got to adapt.

990
01:03:29,470 --> 01:03:32,462
No, I gave you instructions,
and you know the consequences!

991
01:03:32,640 --> 01:03:34,107
I mean, don't you have a plan B?

992
01:03:34,275 --> 01:03:36,300
No, plan B is enforcing plan A!

993
01:03:36,477 --> 01:03:39,605
And the minute you stop believing me,
motherfucker, that's it!

994
01:03:39,780 --> 01:03:42,578
I believe you, you gotta believe
and understand those cops...

995
01:03:42,750 --> 01:03:45,116
...are gonna be down
and next to you any second--

996
01:03:45,286 --> 01:03:47,948
Bring it, man! Let them
unload their guns, I don't care!

997
01:03:48,122 --> 01:03:50,386
And what's the point of that?
What's the point?

998
01:03:50,558 --> 01:03:52,992
I told you we all owe God a death.

999
01:03:53,160 --> 01:03:56,061
And now it's two minutes
past the deadline, two minutes.

1000
01:03:56,230 --> 01:03:59,461
Which means two people,
almost three, have to go.

1001
01:03:59,633 --> 01:04:00,964
They have to die.

1002
01:04:03,604 --> 01:04:05,868
The money's there, Ryder.
Nobody else has to die.

1003
01:04:06,040 --> 01:04:07,064
The money's there.

1004
01:04:07,241 --> 01:04:11,507
I don't know what you owe God. I can
tell you, you can't pay him in cash.

1005
01:04:13,514 --> 01:04:15,880
You never see a U-Haul
behind a hearse, Ryder.

1006
01:04:16,050 --> 01:04:19,577
The Egyptians tried it. It doesn't work.
You can't take the money with you.

1007
01:04:21,255 --> 01:04:22,688
Ryder?

1008
01:04:23,424 --> 01:04:25,016
You can't take the money with you.

1009
01:04:25,760 --> 01:04:29,662
All this talk of God,
I think I need to pray.

1010
01:04:29,830 --> 01:04:31,559
Give me a minute.

1011
01:04:34,835 --> 01:04:35,859
I can do that.

1012
01:04:41,976 --> 01:04:43,341
You did good, Walter.

1013
01:04:47,481 --> 01:04:49,574
What's the reality of getting in,
ending this?

1014
01:04:49,750 --> 01:04:52,082
We'd have to be willing to accept
heavy casualties.

1015
01:04:52,253 --> 01:04:54,153
It's a hard choice, but I say make it.

1016
01:04:54,321 --> 01:04:58,451
New York City does not have
an acceptable casualty rate.

1017
01:04:58,626 --> 01:05:00,560
This is your area,
what do you suggest?

1018
01:05:00,728 --> 01:05:03,925
We should buy time. So far this
son of a bitch hasn't allowed us to.

1019
01:05:04,098 --> 01:05:06,225
This might be the first time
we got through.

1020
01:05:06,400 --> 01:05:08,960
Trust your man? He confessed
to a felony 20 minutes ago.

1021
01:05:09,136 --> 01:05:12,230
There are people down there
who are alive because of him.

1022
01:05:12,406 --> 01:05:14,465
Until we change the rules
or hope runs out...

1023
01:05:14,642 --> 01:05:17,406
...we should stick with the situation
we have now.

1024
01:05:18,813 --> 01:05:20,246
Do what you need to do.

1025
01:05:31,625 --> 01:05:33,252
Hey, Garber, you there?

1026
01:05:33,861 --> 01:05:35,920
-Yeah, I'm here.
-Speak up.

1027
01:05:36,096 --> 01:05:37,723
I'm here.

1028
01:05:38,599 --> 01:05:41,090
-I talked to God.
-That's good. What did he say?

1029
01:05:41,268 --> 01:05:43,964
He said I should trust in him.
All others, pay cash.

1030
01:05:44,138 --> 01:05:46,402
How soon can you get it down here?

1031
01:05:47,741 --> 01:05:51,177
From that station, it would take them
about five minutes to walk it down.

1032
01:05:51,345 --> 01:05:53,575
-No can do.
-About 10 minutes to walk it down.

1033
01:05:53,747 --> 01:05:55,044
No, no, no, I mean you, man.

1034
01:05:55,216 --> 01:05:57,343
How long would it take you
to come down here?

1035
01:05:58,419 --> 01:06:00,011
Don't understand.
What do you mean?

1036
01:06:00,187 --> 01:06:01,745
I mean you. I wanna meet you.

1037
01:06:01,922 --> 01:06:05,016
And if you bring it,
I know the cops aren't bringing it.

1038
01:06:05,993 --> 01:06:08,757
Well, you know, I don't know
how I'm gonna carry that money.

1039
01:06:08,929 --> 01:06:11,363
-lt must weigh....
-Two-hundred and twenty pounds.

1040
01:06:11,532 --> 01:06:13,295
Stick it in a wheelbarrow
or something.

1041
01:06:13,467 --> 01:06:15,731
Why are we discussing weight?
Shouldn't you think:

1042
01:06:15,903 --> 01:06:19,100
-"Get the fuck out of there"?
-Okay, get the fuck out of there.

1043
01:06:19,273 --> 01:06:22,174
Good, that's progress.
Now, look, plan B. Your idea.

1044
01:06:22,343 --> 01:06:25,642
And part of plan B is you, Garber,
deliver that money...

1045
01:06:25,813 --> 01:06:28,646
...or I kill another hostage,
you got that?

1046
01:06:32,019 --> 01:06:34,544
You got seven minutes, buddy boy.

1047
01:06:41,829 --> 01:06:45,526
You got six minutes and 55 seconds,
check me.

1048
01:06:47,501 --> 01:06:48,525
Do it!

1049
01:06:50,371 --> 01:06:51,395
I check.

1050
01:06:51,572 --> 01:06:55,508
And tell that sleazebag negotiator
to call me when you've got the money.

1051
01:06:59,213 --> 01:07:00,976
You don't have to do this.

1052
01:07:26,040 --> 01:07:29,168
Finally somebody got their head
out of their ass, huh?

1053
01:07:34,348 --> 01:07:35,372
Hello?

1054
01:07:35,549 --> 01:07:37,881
Hey, how you doing, baby?
What are you doing?

1055
01:07:38,819 --> 01:07:42,346
What do you mean, what am I doing?
I'm watching the thing, the hostages.

1056
01:07:42,523 --> 01:07:45,890
They mentioned you. They said a
dispatcher was talking to the terrorists.

1057
01:07:46,060 --> 01:07:47,925
Yeah, yeah, they're not terrorists.

1058
01:07:48,329 --> 01:07:50,422
They are if they're down there
waving guns.

1059
01:07:50,597 --> 01:07:52,997
Right, right.
Listen, Therese, are you listening?

1060
01:07:53,167 --> 01:07:56,694
-I'm listening.
-Look, I'm the one that--

1061
01:07:56,870 --> 01:07:59,566
You're right. I was the one
that's been talking to them.

1062
01:08:00,274 --> 01:08:03,471
I knew it. I am so proud of you.

1063
01:08:03,644 --> 01:08:06,112
After everything, all this,
them trying to fire you.

1064
01:08:06,280 --> 01:08:08,407
Them sticking you
in a dispatch job and you--

1065
01:08:09,483 --> 01:08:10,643
Where are you?

1066
01:08:10,818 --> 01:08:12,979
I'm at a heliport.

1067
01:08:13,153 --> 01:08:15,121
I'm getting ready
to get on a helicopter...

1068
01:08:15,289 --> 01:08:19,487
...because they want me to take
the money down to the tunnel.

1069
01:08:19,660 --> 01:08:22,891
What? Are they crazy?

1070
01:08:23,063 --> 01:08:25,725
-It's real simple. There's nothing to it.
-Over there.

1071
01:08:25,899 --> 01:08:29,562
What it is, is he knows I'm not a cop,
so he wants me to come down--

1072
01:08:29,737 --> 01:08:31,967
Is it all right if I wait here?
Can I wait here?

1073
01:08:32,139 --> 01:08:35,472
They need me to take the money down
because they know I'm not a cop...

1074
01:08:35,642 --> 01:08:39,476
...and, you know, they're saying
that he might kill somebody, honey.

1075
01:08:39,646 --> 01:08:42,615
Well, then somebody has to die,
because you can't.

1076
01:08:42,783 --> 01:08:44,250
He's talking to his wife.

1077
01:08:44,418 --> 01:08:46,613
I understand, baby.
Listen to me. Listen to me.

1078
01:08:46,787 --> 01:08:48,755
-Just tell Angela at the meet--
-Let's go!

1079
01:08:48,922 --> 01:08:50,480
When she runs over the hurdles.

1080
01:08:50,657 --> 01:08:52,716
Tell her to run straight through
the hurdles.

1081
01:08:52,893 --> 01:08:56,294
-Just like I always tell her, okay?
-Come on, we gotta go.

1082
01:08:56,463 --> 01:08:58,522
You tell her yourself.

1083
01:08:58,699 --> 01:09:00,792
-Now, you listen to me.
-Yeah, I'm listening.

1084
01:09:00,968 --> 01:09:04,369
Now, you do what you have to do,
but we need milk.

1085
01:09:04,538 --> 01:09:06,870
So on your way home,
I want you to bring a gallon.

1086
01:09:07,041 --> 01:09:09,373
Of milk? Okay.

1087
01:09:09,543 --> 01:09:10,942
You promise.

1088
01:09:11,111 --> 01:09:13,602
Why do we--? Why a gallon?
Why not a half a gallon?

1089
01:09:13,781 --> 01:09:16,477
Just bring a gallon. A gallon.

1090
01:09:16,917 --> 01:09:18,908
Okay. Okay.

1091
01:09:19,086 --> 01:09:22,419
I can get a half a gallon,
I'll get a half a gallon.

1092
01:09:23,023 --> 01:09:24,285
I gotta go.

1093
01:09:28,128 --> 01:09:29,618
All right, thanks, guys.

1094
01:09:45,279 --> 01:09:47,747
Put your-- Put your headset on.

1095
01:09:58,859 --> 01:10:03,353
You ever do anything like this before?
You know, go in unarmed?

1096
01:10:03,530 --> 01:10:05,589
Yeah. Two years ago, Brooklyn.

1097
01:10:05,766 --> 01:10:09,429
Flatbush Avenue.
I got the hostages out.

1098
01:10:12,272 --> 01:10:13,432
And the guy with the gun?

1099
01:10:14,908 --> 01:10:17,843
The guy with the gun,
didn't end well for him.

1100
01:10:18,278 --> 01:10:20,872
-For the guy with the gun?
-Yeah.

1101
01:10:26,687 --> 01:10:29,417
It's nice seeing it
from this perspective, huh?

1102
01:10:30,390 --> 01:10:32,415
You can see what you're fighting for.

1103
01:10:47,708 --> 01:10:50,074
I love you so much.

1104
01:10:53,380 --> 01:10:54,404
Did you hear me?

1105
01:10:55,415 --> 01:10:56,905
Yeah.

1106
01:11:01,054 --> 01:11:03,284
Well, do you love me back?

1107
01:11:03,790 --> 01:11:06,088
Can't really talk right now.

1108
01:11:11,632 --> 01:11:13,930
All you have to say is "Yes. "

1109
01:11:14,101 --> 01:11:16,569
That's a lot less words than saying,
"l can't talk. "

1110
01:11:21,975 --> 01:11:25,069
I'm having a really weird
fucking day.

1111
01:11:27,981 --> 01:11:30,040
Oh, God.

1112
01:11:30,217 --> 01:11:33,618
If we'd anticipated this,
we could have made a lot of money.

1113
01:11:37,624 --> 01:11:39,251
What kind of guy
would you expect...

1114
01:11:39,426 --> 01:11:41,621
...to take a model to lceland
for the weekend?

1115
01:11:41,795 --> 01:11:43,695
-An ass model.
-An ass model.

1116
01:11:44,965 --> 01:11:47,160
-A Wall Street guy.
-A Wall Street guy.

1117
01:11:54,841 --> 01:11:56,502
He's here!

1118
01:11:56,944 --> 01:11:59,378
The one-hour time limit
reported earlier has expired.

1119
01:11:59,546 --> 01:12:04,040
We're not sure who this is. It could
be hostage negotiators or detectives.

1120
01:12:04,218 --> 01:12:06,753
Once we have any updates,
we'll be back to you live.

1121
01:12:14,194 --> 01:12:15,388
-Camonetti.
-How are you?

1122
01:12:15,562 --> 01:12:17,655
-Mr. Garber, Lieutenant Staley.
-Pleasure.

1123
01:12:17,831 --> 01:12:20,493
-You got a radio set up to the train?
-Set up right there.

1124
01:12:20,667 --> 01:12:22,931
You can talk to the train
or to Rail Control.

1125
01:12:23,103 --> 01:12:26,539
Okay. Just do what he says,
and remember everything you see.

1126
01:12:26,707 --> 01:12:28,197
Let's go.

1127
01:12:30,444 --> 01:12:32,503
So who the hell did you fuck
to get this job?

1128
01:12:32,679 --> 01:12:35,147
Myself. It was easier than it looked.

1129
01:12:35,315 --> 01:12:38,079
Yeah, fucking yourself always is.

1130
01:12:41,488 --> 01:12:44,924
Pelham 123, come in.
Pelham 123, come in.

1131
01:12:45,092 --> 01:12:46,218
Who am I talking to?

1132
01:12:46,393 --> 01:12:49,487
This is Lieutenant Camonetti.
We spoke earlier.

1133
01:12:49,663 --> 01:12:52,757
Yeah, you're the greaseball.
What'd you do, go out for a pizza?

1134
01:12:52,933 --> 01:12:54,764
What's my money doing, man?
Where is it?

1135
01:12:54,935 --> 01:12:58,735
Mr. Garber is in the tunnel.
The money is two minutes away.

1136
01:12:58,905 --> 01:13:00,964
Oh, Garber, man.
That is a dependable man.

1137
01:13:01,141 --> 01:13:02,665
He's a good man too.

1138
01:13:02,843 --> 01:13:04,708
Absolutely. How about you, Ryder?

1139
01:13:04,878 --> 01:13:07,244
Everybody's got some good in them,
don't you think?

1140
01:13:07,414 --> 01:13:09,314
Is this where
you try to get through to me?

1141
01:13:09,483 --> 01:13:12,884
I don't think so, motherfucker.
Now I got three instructions for you.

1142
01:13:13,053 --> 01:13:15,146
Number one,
when this conversation is over...

1143
01:13:15,322 --> 01:13:18,223
...I want you to restore the power
to the whole sector.

1144
01:13:18,392 --> 01:13:20,792
Number two,
I want you to clear the local tracks...

1145
01:13:20,961 --> 01:13:23,327
...from 68th Street
down to Coney lsland.

1146
01:13:23,497 --> 01:13:25,829
And when I say, "Clear, "
I don't wanna see no cops.

1147
01:13:25,999 --> 01:13:27,398
I want all the lights green.

1148
01:13:27,567 --> 01:13:29,432
Don't trip me up with a red,
got that?

1149
01:13:29,603 --> 01:13:30,763
Absolutely.

1150
01:13:30,937 --> 01:13:33,997
And number three,
don't play games with me...

1151
01:13:34,174 --> 01:13:38,440
...or I'll track you down and I'll fuck you
in your greaseball ass, motherfucker!

1152
01:13:40,247 --> 01:13:41,612
Over and out.

1153
01:13:45,252 --> 01:13:46,810
Let's go.

1154
01:13:51,725 --> 01:13:52,749
All right.

1155
01:13:52,926 --> 01:13:55,360
-Know how to use one of these?
-No.

1156
01:13:55,529 --> 01:13:57,394
It's really simple. Okay?

1157
01:13:57,564 --> 01:13:59,896
Safety's on, safety's off.

1158
01:14:00,067 --> 01:14:01,364
On, off.

1159
01:14:01,535 --> 01:14:04,231
Aim at anything you don't like,
you pull the trigger.

1160
01:14:04,404 --> 01:14:07,066
-What if they frisk me?
-We got that covered.

1161
01:14:08,909 --> 01:14:10,900
-That's it?
-That's it.

1162
01:14:12,279 --> 01:14:13,746
It's got a false bottom.

1163
01:14:13,914 --> 01:14:16,678
It's gonna be this one. You got that?

1164
01:14:17,651 --> 01:14:19,642
-I got it.
-Good.

1165
01:14:20,120 --> 01:14:21,519
Don't worry about it.

1166
01:14:22,689 --> 01:14:24,623
Just don't fuck it up.

1167
01:14:29,663 --> 01:14:30,960
Okay.

1168
01:14:31,131 --> 01:14:33,156
We got an lD on Ryder.

1169
01:14:33,734 --> 01:14:37,295
Dennis Ford. He was released from
Clinton Correctional two weeks ago.

1170
01:14:37,471 --> 01:14:38,836
Did a nine-year stretch.

1171
01:14:39,005 --> 01:14:41,530
The last four on the same cell block
as Phil Ramos.

1172
01:14:41,775 --> 01:14:44,300
His name shows up
on an lcelandic Air passenger list...

1173
01:14:44,478 --> 01:14:47,345
...in September of 1998,
right after Fashion Week.

1174
01:14:48,048 --> 01:14:50,312
Dennis Ford. You remember?

1175
01:14:50,484 --> 01:14:53,044
We used his case when
he was running as an example of--

1176
01:14:53,220 --> 01:14:56,747
The kind of nonsense that we would
clean up if I got elected mayor, yeah.

1177
01:14:56,923 --> 01:14:58,254
He ran a private equity firm.

1178
01:14:58,425 --> 01:15:00,325
His biggest client
was the pension fund.

1179
01:15:00,494 --> 01:15:02,553
-He siphoned off....
-Twenty-million dollars.

1180
01:15:02,729 --> 01:15:05,425
He did a plea bargain for three.
The judge gave him 10.

1181
01:15:05,599 --> 01:15:07,624
Maybe that's why he's so pissed off.

1182
01:15:07,801 --> 01:15:11,362
Judge gave him 10 years because we
didn't recover all of the city's money.

1183
01:15:11,538 --> 01:15:13,506
Couple million unaccounted for.
Seed money.

1184
01:15:13,673 --> 01:15:14,799
Seed money? For what?

1185
01:15:14,975 --> 01:15:18,809
For today, you play the terrorist card,
you panic the market into a drop.

1186
01:15:18,979 --> 01:15:21,743
You know it's coming, you make
a great deal with $2 million.

1187
01:15:21,915 --> 01:15:24,179
-What about the hostage money?
-That's nothing...

1188
01:15:24,351 --> 01:15:27,843
...compared to the money you could
make. Let's get downtown to the SEC.

1189
01:15:28,021 --> 01:15:30,251
Check the trades,
especially the put options.

1190
01:15:45,539 --> 01:15:48,531
-Good luck, Garber.
-See you when you get back.

1191
01:15:54,514 --> 01:15:56,539
We got company.

1192
01:16:11,264 --> 01:16:12,288
Garber.

1193
01:16:12,799 --> 01:16:16,530
When you put your socks on
this morning, did you ever think...?

1194
01:16:18,438 --> 01:16:20,372
Turn around, let him frisk you.

1195
01:16:23,477 --> 01:16:26,378
I was worried about you.
I thought maybe you'd get lost...

1196
01:16:26,546 --> 01:16:29,014
...but then I remembered
you were a motorman, so....

1197
01:16:29,182 --> 01:16:31,776
These tunnels don't change much,
do they?

1198
01:16:31,952 --> 01:16:33,544
Just the people in them.

1199
01:16:36,990 --> 01:16:38,958
-Are we good?
-It's here. We're good.

1200
01:16:39,125 --> 01:16:40,456
All right, come on up.

1201
01:16:41,561 --> 01:16:43,119
Let's go.

1202
01:17:04,117 --> 01:17:07,086
Damn.
You're taller than I thought you'd be.

1203
01:17:07,254 --> 01:17:09,916
You're good-looking too.
Come on, sit down.

1204
01:17:10,690 --> 01:17:11,918
It's nice to meet you.

1205
01:17:26,172 --> 01:17:28,140
What do you weigh,
about, what, 220?

1206
01:17:29,075 --> 01:17:32,533
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
220 on a good day.

1207
01:17:34,915 --> 01:17:36,780
Oh, that's Ramos.

1208
01:17:37,517 --> 01:17:41,044
He's what you would have called
the brains in the operation.

1209
01:17:42,856 --> 01:17:44,221
Dumb fuck.

1210
01:17:48,795 --> 01:17:51,593
So how long has it been
since you've driven one of these?

1211
01:17:55,335 --> 01:17:58,099
-That's why you brought me here?
-You're a motorman, right?

1212
01:17:58,271 --> 01:18:00,136
Once a motorman,
always a motorman.

1213
01:18:01,074 --> 01:18:04,043
You play your cards right,
you might get a part of the cut.

1214
01:18:17,824 --> 01:18:19,382
Well, this is--

1215
01:18:19,960 --> 01:18:22,451
It's a new train.
I'm not certified on the new trains.

1216
01:18:22,629 --> 01:18:25,962
Well, I got faith in you, man.
But I'm going to ask you one question.

1217
01:18:26,132 --> 01:18:28,999
You know, that thing when you
told your wife about the 35 K...

1218
01:18:29,169 --> 01:18:30,227
...how did she react?

1219
01:18:31,037 --> 01:18:33,096
-We gotta talk about--?
-Don't be sensitive.

1220
01:18:33,273 --> 01:18:35,400
-I'm not being--
-Did she freak out or what?

1221
01:18:35,575 --> 01:18:37,839
She wasn't happy,
but she understood.

1222
01:18:38,011 --> 01:18:39,273
Well, that's love, right?

1223
01:18:39,446 --> 01:18:41,937
No, that's marriage.
That's another thing.

1224
01:18:42,849 --> 01:18:44,680
You think they're gonna move
that train?

1225
01:18:44,851 --> 01:18:48,446
Seems like a possibility. How are we
with street-level, emergency exits?

1226
01:18:48,622 --> 01:18:49,782
I got a blanket.

1227
01:18:49,956 --> 01:18:53,392
I got radio cars and a man
at every exit from 42nd to South Ferry.

1228
01:18:53,827 --> 01:18:55,454
We gotta go.

1229
01:18:55,695 --> 01:18:57,663
Hey, Camonetti.

1230
01:18:58,098 --> 01:18:59,395
Fucking greaseball, man.

1231
01:19:00,133 --> 01:19:02,328
Hey, greaseball, speak up.

1232
01:19:02,502 --> 01:19:04,800
I see red. I don't see green.

1233
01:19:04,971 --> 01:19:06,939
What's taking so fucking long?

1234
01:19:07,107 --> 01:19:08,472
Blanket is not tucked in yet.

1235
01:19:08,642 --> 01:19:11,076
Stall him. I need two minutes,
buy me two minutes.

1236
01:19:11,244 --> 01:19:12,711
Haven't cleared the tracks yet.

1237
01:19:12,879 --> 01:19:16,042
Mr. Ryder, we'll be up and ready
in less than two minutes.

1238
01:19:16,216 --> 01:19:18,081
We're gonna move forward here,
okay?

1239
01:19:18,251 --> 01:19:21,015
We're gonna move forward,
and if we get onto a red signal...

1240
01:19:21,187 --> 01:19:22,484
...and the brakes trip up...

1241
01:19:22,656 --> 01:19:25,386
...your friend Walter Garber's
getting it in the head.

1242
01:19:27,761 --> 01:19:30,389
-You got it?
-Yes, sir. I got it.

1243
01:19:30,563 --> 01:19:31,825
Let's roll, let's roll.

1244
01:19:33,266 --> 01:19:34,665
Hope you were bluffing.

1245
01:19:34,834 --> 01:19:37,894
Yeah, I'm bluffing, man.
You gotta say what you gotta say.

1246
01:19:39,973 --> 01:19:42,965
You thought by coming down here,
you'd be redeemed, didn't you?

1247
01:19:43,143 --> 01:19:45,168
God bless you, Garber.

1248
01:19:46,379 --> 01:19:48,643
You're more fucked up than I am.

1249
01:19:49,215 --> 01:19:51,843
At least the same fucked up.

1250
01:19:52,085 --> 01:19:53,848
Come on, let's go, let's go, let's go.

1251
01:20:00,026 --> 01:20:01,186
Let's go.

1252
01:20:11,171 --> 01:20:12,365
She's on the move.

1253
01:20:16,810 --> 01:20:18,573
Put some speed on it.

1254
01:20:25,185 --> 01:20:27,881
He's by me, headed south.
Male, black, at the controls.

1255
01:20:34,360 --> 01:20:35,725
Motherfuckers.

1256
01:20:35,895 --> 01:20:39,626
You're playing with fire, my man.
I wanna see them green.

1257
01:20:39,799 --> 01:20:42,734
Turn to green or I'll put a hole
in Garber's head right now.

1258
01:20:42,902 --> 01:20:44,426
-Do it!
-We believe you.

1259
01:20:44,604 --> 01:20:46,299
We're moving as fast as we can.

1260
01:20:46,473 --> 01:20:50,136
-What happens if they run a red light?
-lt'll trip the brakes.

1261
01:20:50,310 --> 01:20:51,709
Coming up on the first one.

1262
01:20:54,881 --> 01:20:58,146
There, that's what I'm looking for.
That's what I'm looking for.

1263
01:20:58,618 --> 01:20:59,846
Here he comes, right now.

1264
01:21:13,032 --> 01:21:15,330
Garber's driving the train.
Sniper confirmed it.

1265
01:21:15,502 --> 01:21:18,232
What are you saying, he's
in on it? There ain't no way.

1266
01:21:18,404 --> 01:21:20,395
Sniper killed Ramos,
he was their driver...

1267
01:21:20,573 --> 01:21:22,336
...they probably need Garber
to drive.

1268
01:21:30,917 --> 01:21:34,978
They get to Coney lsland, they hit the
trippers and the brakes will come on.

1269
01:21:39,492 --> 01:21:40,891
-ls that 33rd?
-Yes, sir.

1270
01:21:41,060 --> 01:21:43,585
-How far to the signal?
-About a tenth of a mile.

1271
01:21:43,763 --> 01:21:46,698
You stop when we get there.
We're moving out. You got that?

1272
01:21:46,866 --> 01:21:48,265
I'm slowing down now.

1273
01:21:56,876 --> 01:21:57,968
Are they slowing down?

1274
01:21:58,144 --> 01:22:00,374
They have to.
They're coming up to a signal point.

1275
01:22:05,652 --> 01:22:07,085
What is that?

1276
01:22:07,253 --> 01:22:09,221
You're the old motorman,
you tell me.

1277
01:22:24,204 --> 01:22:27,503
-She stopped just below 33rd Street.
-What the hell are they doing?

1278
01:22:27,674 --> 01:22:29,198
Oh, jeez.

1279
01:22:29,375 --> 01:22:30,467
Why that little stop?

1280
01:22:30,643 --> 01:22:32,508
Train has to stop at signal points.

1281
01:22:32,679 --> 01:22:33,941
Some kind of an override?

1282
01:22:34,113 --> 01:22:37,105
Yep, some kind of an override,
that's right.

1283
01:22:37,283 --> 01:22:41,151
There we go.
Okay, let's move out. Let's go, let's go.

1284
01:23:07,213 --> 01:23:08,976
Roosevelt tunnel, which way?

1285
01:23:10,216 --> 01:23:11,979
Which way?

1286
01:23:17,824 --> 01:23:19,951
She's moving again.
Next stop, 28th Street.

1287
01:23:20,426 --> 01:23:21,825
Why that little stop, huh?

1288
01:23:21,995 --> 01:23:24,327
-I told you, the signal points.
-How do you know...

1289
01:23:24,497 --> 01:23:27,557
-...they didn't set the throttle, jump?
-We got every exit covered.

1290
01:23:27,734 --> 01:23:29,099
There's nowhere to go.

1291
01:23:29,269 --> 01:23:31,703
Listen, the throttle can't be set.
It has to be held.

1292
01:23:31,871 --> 01:23:33,998
It's the failsafe,
it's a dead-man's switch.

1293
01:23:34,173 --> 01:23:36,198
Doesn't have a hand
pressing down on it...

1294
01:23:36,376 --> 01:23:39,504
...the train stops cold.
Believe me, they're still aboard.

1295
01:23:48,821 --> 01:23:50,049
It's going faster.

1296
01:23:59,399 --> 01:24:01,560
Emri, off the track. Come on.

1297
01:24:19,452 --> 01:24:20,646
Let's go!

1298
01:24:23,256 --> 01:24:25,315
Garber, come on.

1299
01:24:27,093 --> 01:24:28,890
Come on!

1300
01:24:40,106 --> 01:24:42,404
It's gonna derail
before it gets to Coney lsland.

1301
01:24:46,212 --> 01:24:48,544
That's it. That's it right there.
Roosevelt tunnel.

1302
01:24:51,451 --> 01:24:54,011
It's a fucking train crossover.
Come on. Cross over now!

1303
01:24:54,187 --> 01:24:56,621
-What?
-Come on, move!

1304
01:25:01,561 --> 01:25:02,789
Hey!

1305
01:25:16,909 --> 01:25:19,810
-Fuck it, let's go!
-We gotta find him!

1306
01:25:19,979 --> 01:25:22,413
We don't have time! Let's go!

1307
01:25:39,365 --> 01:25:41,492
I love you. I fucking love you.

1308
01:25:41,667 --> 01:25:43,794
Geo, I fucking love you too.

1309
01:25:57,283 --> 01:26:00,377
Hello? Hello?

1310
01:27:13,826 --> 01:27:14,850
We're getting calls.

1311
01:27:15,027 --> 01:27:17,461
Cops on the platform
are seeing passengers...

1312
01:27:17,630 --> 01:27:21,259
-...nobody in the motorman's booth.
-Believe me, they're still aboard.

1313
01:27:24,103 --> 01:27:26,298
It's all right!
As soon as we hit a red light...

1314
01:27:26,472 --> 01:27:30,067
-...the brakes will stop it automatically.
-Yeah, but they're all green!

1315
01:28:36,876 --> 01:28:38,036
Four stops away.

1316
01:28:49,655 --> 01:28:50,883
Two stops.

1317
01:29:04,503 --> 01:29:06,562
Oh, Jesus. The train just stopped.

1318
01:29:14,947 --> 01:29:17,074
I really gotta take that piss.

1319
01:29:18,884 --> 01:29:21,944
There's no hijackers onboard,
just passengers.

1320
01:29:23,022 --> 01:29:24,990
Where was that first stop
that they made?

1321
01:29:25,157 --> 01:29:26,385
Near 34th.

1322
01:29:27,159 --> 01:29:29,059
-That's by the Roosevelt spur.
-The what?

1323
01:29:29,228 --> 01:29:32,254
A derelict tunnel
built under the Waldorf Hotel.

1324
01:29:32,431 --> 01:29:36,060
Converge everything on that area.
Throw a goddamn dragnet over it!

1325
01:30:09,602 --> 01:30:11,194
Hey!

1326
01:30:21,647 --> 01:30:23,308
Freeze!

1327
01:30:36,929 --> 01:30:38,624
Put your hands in the air!

1328
01:31:01,087 --> 01:31:02,611
Hey!

1329
01:31:03,055 --> 01:31:04,613
Hey!

1330
01:31:06,359 --> 01:31:09,522
Hey. Get out, get out, get out.

1331
01:31:10,262 --> 01:31:11,354
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

1332
01:31:12,064 --> 01:31:13,361
I'm sorry.

1333
01:31:44,964 --> 01:31:46,659
Out of the-- Get out of the way!

1334
01:32:04,350 --> 01:32:05,578
Just go, go, go.

1335
01:32:32,845 --> 01:32:34,676
-911 operator.
-Hello? Hello?

1336
01:32:34,847 --> 01:32:37,543
-This is Walter Garber, MTA.
-How do you spell that?

1337
01:32:37,716 --> 01:32:39,411
Don't worry about how to spell it.

1338
01:32:39,585 --> 01:32:41,450
Just tell Lieutenant Camonetti...

1339
01:32:41,620 --> 01:32:44,020
...that Ryder is headed
to the Manhattan Bridge!

1340
01:33:24,497 --> 01:33:28,058
Cars everywhere. Nobody's
going anywhere for a long time.

1341
01:33:36,041 --> 01:33:37,133
Hey. Hey!

1342
01:33:39,945 --> 01:33:41,674
-ls he in there?
-No, no, no.

1343
01:33:41,847 --> 01:33:43,144
-No.
-Where did he go?

1344
01:33:43,315 --> 01:33:46,751
Brooklyn. He said he couldn't wait,
he started walking.

1345
01:33:46,919 --> 01:33:48,511
This fucking city!

1346
01:34:22,855 --> 01:34:24,618
Come on, you guys. Move out!

1347
01:34:34,567 --> 01:34:36,228
Ryder!

1348
01:34:39,838 --> 01:34:40,998
Don't move.

1349
01:34:42,408 --> 01:34:45,070
So is this how you thought
the day was going to end, huh?

1350
01:34:45,244 --> 01:34:47,212
When you put your socks on
this morning?

1351
01:34:47,379 --> 01:34:49,370
This make you feel better, Garber?

1352
01:34:50,549 --> 01:34:52,517
That make everything okay now?

1353
01:34:52,685 --> 01:34:54,915
No! But it's a start.

1354
01:34:58,157 --> 01:34:59,988
Don't move.

1355
01:35:22,548 --> 01:35:24,516
Don't move!

1356
01:35:27,186 --> 01:35:28,551
Hey!

1357
01:35:30,289 --> 01:35:33,588
Garber Baby boy,
I ain't going back to prison.

1358
01:35:33,759 --> 01:35:38,128
I don't-- I don't think you got any--
Any options now or leverage.

1359
01:35:39,698 --> 01:35:40,892
Hey!

1360
01:35:43,335 --> 01:35:44,734
Hey!

1361
01:35:44,903 --> 01:35:47,463
We all owe God a death,
I told you that.

1362
01:35:47,640 --> 01:35:49,608
You're wrong, Ryder.
We owe God life.

1363
01:35:49,775 --> 01:35:52,403
Life. And that's the life
I gave you back today.

1364
01:35:52,578 --> 01:35:54,739
And now you have to
give me something back.

1365
01:35:57,616 --> 01:35:59,516
What are you talking about?

1366
01:35:59,952 --> 01:36:03,046
You got a gun in your hand,
I want you to use it. Shoot me.

1367
01:36:03,222 --> 01:36:07,283
No, shoot me before they shoot me,
or I'm gonna kill you.

1368
01:36:08,160 --> 01:36:10,924
I will shoot you.
I don't want to, but I will.

1369
01:36:11,096 --> 01:36:12,393
-Hey!
-I thought you cared.

1370
01:36:12,564 --> 01:36:13,622
-No!
-You said:

1371
01:36:13,799 --> 01:36:16,734
"Ryder. Ryder,
don't you have anyone who cares?"

1372
01:36:16,902 --> 01:36:17,994
I thought that was you.

1373
01:36:18,170 --> 01:36:20,730
-Come on, man, pay it back.
-I'm not gonna shoot you.

1374
01:36:20,906 --> 01:36:22,771
I'm gonna give you 10,
then deal's off.

1375
01:36:22,941 --> 01:36:26,274
I got a gun, I'm gonna use it.
I'm gonna take your life back.

1376
01:36:27,913 --> 01:36:30,143
-Hey!
-Come on, man!

1377
01:36:30,315 --> 01:36:35,844
Ten, nine, eight, seven, six, five--

1378
01:36:36,021 --> 01:36:39,218
You gonna take this down to zero?
Come on, motherfucker, shoot me!

1379
01:36:39,391 --> 01:36:41,518
I am not going to shoot you!

1380
01:36:42,695 --> 01:36:45,425
Five, four. Come on.

1381
01:36:45,597 --> 01:36:47,690
-Hey!
-Three.

1382
01:36:47,966 --> 01:36:49,297
Police, drop your weapon!

1383
01:36:49,468 --> 01:36:51,936
I'm disappointed in you. Two.

1384
01:37:01,947 --> 01:37:04,108
You're my goddamn hero.

1385
01:37:15,294 --> 01:37:17,159
Drop your weapon!

1386
01:38:02,307 --> 01:38:04,002
Mr. Garber.

1387
01:38:06,311 --> 01:38:08,472
-lnteresting day, huh?
-Yes, sir.

1388
01:38:08,647 --> 01:38:11,172
You know, just about every day
I make a speech...

1389
01:38:11,350 --> 01:38:13,580
...and it starts with:

1390
01:38:13,752 --> 01:38:17,313
"I'd like to thank you on behalf of
the city of New York," blah, blah, blah.

1391
01:38:17,489 --> 01:38:20,185
And I never know
who I'm thanking or why.

1392
01:38:20,659 --> 01:38:21,751
But you...

1393
01:38:23,028 --> 01:38:24,552
...did a hell of a thing today.

1394
01:38:24,730 --> 01:38:27,028
You went to bat
for the city of New York.

1395
01:38:27,199 --> 01:38:30,134
And on behalf of me,
I'd like to thank you.

1396
01:38:31,069 --> 01:38:34,163
Well, you're welcome.
I mean, it's been an amazing day.

1397
01:38:34,339 --> 01:38:37,740
Everybody's thanking me all day,
but I appreciate it. You're welcome.

1398
01:38:38,177 --> 01:38:40,338
And I want you to know...

1399
01:38:40,512 --> 01:38:44,243
...that tomorrow, the city of New York
is going to go to bat for you.

1400
01:38:45,984 --> 01:38:48,452
In a big way. You understand?

1401
01:38:48,620 --> 01:38:49,644
Yes, sir.

1402
01:38:50,589 --> 01:38:52,921
And this city
has a very good batting average.

1403
01:38:53,792 --> 01:38:56,522
-I appreciate it.
-All right.

1404
01:38:57,629 --> 01:38:58,653
I'm gonna get home.

1405
01:38:59,231 --> 01:39:00,493
Oh, take my car.

1406
01:39:00,933 --> 01:39:03,595
-No, no, I'll take--
-Put the siren on and everything.

1407
01:39:03,769 --> 01:39:05,464
-There's a siren on there?
-Yes.

1408
01:39:05,637 --> 01:39:07,764
No, I'll take the subway.
But I appreciate it.

1409
01:39:07,940 --> 01:39:08,964
-Really?
-Yeah.

1410
01:39:09,141 --> 01:39:12,508
You know, me, subway all my life.
I get home faster than you anyway.

